ta out of Baby; later dam of Whitney''s 1900 Futurity winner ''Ballyhoo Bey''), accounting for >150 false-positive 1889-1904 Clipper/newspaper hits.", "analysis_notes": "Excluded as equine proper name (''W. B. Jennings'' Ballyhoo, by Duke of Magenta-Baby''). .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-102.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1891 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
