placing ''Ballyhoo Freaks'' squarely at the 1893 Chicago World''s Columbian Exposition while contrasting ''SIDESHOW TALKERS'' (verbal pitchmen) with ''Ballyhoo Freaks'' (outside platform crowd-gathering performers).", "analysis_notes": "Crisp display type in International Amusement Company classified ad recruiting for the 1893 Chicago World''s Fair. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-103.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1893 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-214', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'Alla gooda', 'contextual_evidence', 'negative_corpus_sweep', 'agent_verified', 1894, '1894-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sweetcloverroman00burn/page/n279/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-214.webp', 51850, '26a7677367bffe5565570fb6f41ffa948eadfdb2dd37b2ba7b976a1984200b9d', '{"id": "CERT-1800-214", "slug": "cert-1800-214", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "Alla gooda", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "negative_corpus_sweep", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1894, "date_display": "1894", "sort_date": "1894-01-01", "short_gloss": "Contextual control: Alla gooda in Clara Louise Burnham, Sweet Clover: A Romance of the White City (Boston & New York: Houghton, Mifflin & Co", "source_publication": "Clara Louise Burnham, Sweet Clover: A Romance of the White City (Boston & New York: Houghton, Mifflin & Co., 1894), Ch. XX ''The Midway Plaisance'', p. 274", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sweetcloverroman00burn/page/n279/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 274 (IA leaf 284)", "verbatim_quote": "monotonously from the booth of the much-vaunted Oriental sweetmeat: — \"Alla gooda bum-bum, / Vera nice candy, / Beautifula bum-bum, / Vera good candy,\" repeated ad libitum by the swarthy Arab presiding. Mildred and Jack glanced into the small interior behind him.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1894, "linguistic_note": "Hypothesis 4 Street-Cry Control: Attested 1893 Cairo hawker cries were pidgin English ''Alla gooda bum-bum'', ''Hot-hot-hot!'', ''baksheesh'', and ''Yanka Doodoo''", "analysis_notes": "Primary scan documenting verbatim 1893 Street in Cairo vendor cries (''Alla gooda bum-bum, Vera nice candy, Beautifula bum-bum'', p. 274, i.e. pidgin ''All good bonbon''; ''Look ou-at for Yanka Doodoo,'' bawled Achmet, the donkey boy, p. 279; corroborated by Lawrence L. Lynch, Against Odds, 1894, p. 244 ''Hot-hot-hot!'' and ''Fine bum-bum''), proving eyewitnesses transcribed Cairo cries phonetically with zero ''ballyhoo'' or ''bi-llahi''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-214.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1894 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-104', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'Ballyhoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1895, '1895-09-28', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1895-09-28_43_30/page/n13/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-104.webp', 164334, '8f30b95e81133639602d7f8f0a215bf997b40295ce9224c8bb1410bd7b78c349', '{"id": "CERT-1800-104", "slug": "cert-1800-104", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "Ballyhoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1895, "date_display": "28 Sep 1895", "sort_date": "1895-09-28", "short_gloss": "Ballyhoo in The New York Clipper, Vol. 43, No. 30 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Sept. 28, 1895)", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper, Vol. 43, No. 30 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Sept. 28, 1895)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1895-09-28_43_30/page/n13/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 43, No. 30, p. 478, col. 2 (IA leaf n13; front masthead leaf n0: ''SEPTEMBER 28, 1895'')", "verbatim_quote": "WANTED. SIDE SHOW PROPERTY of all kinds, also WOMAN WITH SNAKES, MUSICAL NOVELTY for Ballyhoo purposes, Double Deck PAINTINGS, SIDE SHOW TOP, 30x 60ft. Give full particulars in first letter. L. C. DESSERT, Gen''l. Del., Dallas, Texas.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1895, "masthead_year": 1895, "linguistic_note": "Demonstrates Stage (a) acoustic/spectacle function (''MUSICAL NOVELTY for Ballyhoo purposes'' alongside ''SIDE SHOW TOP, 30x60ft.'' and ''Double Deck PAINTINGS'') at the Sept.-Oct. 1895 Dallas Texas State Fair, 52 days before OED3''s Nov. 19, 1895 Atlanta citation.", "analysis_notes": "Verified on Sept. 28, 1895 Clipper masthead and p. 478 classified notice by sideshow manager L. C. Dessert. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-104.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1895 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-105', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'ballyhoos', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1895, '1895-11-25', 'https://gahistoricnewspapers.galileo.usg.edu/lccn/sn89054007/1895-11-25/ed-1/seq-4/', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-105.webp', 135506, '039fc6296340990b3edfc30209103d3366c1323e81a70c130a6d5ec20ed29ef6', '{"id": "CERT-1800-105", "slug": "cert-1800-105", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "ballyhoos", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1895, "date_display": "25 Nov 1895", "sort_date": "1895-11-25", "short_gloss": "ballyhoos in The Hustler of Rome (Rome, GA), Nov. 25, 1895 (quoting Athens News / Augusta Chronicle)", "source_publication": "The Hustler of Rome (Rome, GA), Nov. 25, 1895 (quoting Athens News / Augusta Chronicle)", "source_archive": "Georgia Historic Newspapers (GALILEO / DLG)", "source_url": "https://gahistoricnewspapers.galileo.usg.edu/lccn/sn89054007/1895-11-25/ed-1/seq-4/", "page_and_column": "p. 4, col. 3 (seq-4; front masthead seq-1: ''ROME GEORGIA MONDAY EVENING NOVEMBER 25 1895'')", "verbatim_quote": "The Cronicle says that between the \"ballyhoos\" and coochee-coochee\" dancers the Midway seems to be oftener fined than refined.—Athens News. From recent experiences the denizens of the Midway doubtless know themselves to be both fined and re-fined.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1895, "masthead_year": 1895, "linguistic_note": "Independent Georgia press corroboration of the Nov. 1895 Cotton States and International Exposition Midway crackdown in Atlanta (six days after OED3''s Nov. 19, 1895 Atlanta Journal citation), pairing ''ballyhoos'' directly with ''coochee-coochee'' dancers.", "analysis_notes": "Verified on Rome, GA masthead and p. 4 editorial paragraph. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-105.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1895 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-106', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'Bally Hoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1896, '1896-09-26', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1896-09-26_44_30/page/n11/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-106.webp', 142324, 'e37ed46a0015e1c6c9c3bc00d65949f17ecb733e30bd0d6b509b22119ac1aba6', '{"id": "CERT-1800-106", "slug": "cert-1800-106", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "Bally Hoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1896, "date_display": "26 Sep 1896", "sort_date": "1896-09-26", "short_gloss": "Bally Hoo in The New York Clipper, Vol. 44, No. 30 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Sept. 26, 1896)", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper, Vol. 44, No. 30 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Sept. 26, 1896)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1896-09-26_44_30/page/n11/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 44, No. 30, p. 478, col. 2 (IA leaf n11; front masthead leaf n0: ''SEPTEMBER 26, 1896'')", "verbatim_quote": "SPECIALTIES Of every description wanted for \"Bally Hoo\" Stage, outside the Fair Ground Show. Also First Class Bugler or Cornet Soloist. No night work. State lowest salary. ... F. R. BLITZ, Millie Christine Show, Taunton, Mass.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1896, "masthead_year": 1896, "linguistic_note": "Earliest verified attestation of the architectural compound ''\"Bally Hoo\" Stage'' explicitly localized ''outside the Fair Ground Show'' with a ''Bugler or Cornet Soloist'' to draw the fairground tip (33 years before Green''s 1929/1953 ''bally platform'' entries).", "analysis_notes": "Placed by F. R. Blitz for the famous Millie-Christine Show at Taunton Fair, Mass. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-106.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1896 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-107', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'ballyhoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1898, '1898-03-19', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1898-03-19_46_3/page/n15/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-107.webp', 132346, '40933b31424a40b45ff7af5af39f977eb57eb77c6ab1bca1ff3dc17f67e3c4a2', '{"id": "CERT-1800-107", "slug": "cert-1800-107", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "ballyhoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1898, "date_display": "19 Mar 1898", "sort_date": "1898-03-19", "short_gloss": "ballyhoo in The New York Clipper, Vol. 46, No. 3 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Mar. 19, 1898)", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper, Vol. 46, No. 3 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Mar. 19, 1898)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1898-03-19_46_3/page/n15/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 46, No. 3, p. 52, col. 1 (IA leaf n15; front masthead leaf n0: ''MARCH 19, 1898'')", "verbatim_quote": "WAGON FOR SALE.—A made to order Platform Wagon; raising top; back of seat trunk space, 4x10ft.; lamp, trap and banner boxes below bed; fine ballyhoo gong; just the wagon for medicine or notions; weight, 1,600lb; cost $500; good order. Price, $150. T. M. SAYMAN, St. Louis, Mo.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1898, "masthead_year": 1898, "linguistic_note": "Links sideshow/midway ''ballyhoo'' directly to patent-medicine pitch wagons: St. Louis soap-and-liniment magnate Dr. Thomas M. Sayman equips his platform medicine wagon with a ''fine ballyhoo gong'' to summon street crowds.", "analysis_notes": "Verified physical ink ''fine ballyhoo gong'' (correcting raw OCR ''yong'') on p. 52. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-107.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1898 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-108', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'Ballyhoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1898, '1898-04-23', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1898-04-23_46_8/page/n15/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-108.webp', 166498, '8fae211bc70dec7ee0d77d46753ab67f2b0745b12699cf40833178d33dd02183', '{"id": "CERT-1800-108", "slug": "cert-1800-108", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "Ballyhoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1898, "date_display": "23 Apr 1898", "sort_date": "1898-04-23", "short_gloss": "Ballyhoo in The New York Clipper, Vol. 46, No. 8 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Apr. 23, 1898)", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper, Vol. 46, No. 8 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Apr. 23, 1898)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1898-04-23_46_8/page/n15/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 46, No. 8, p. 134, col. 2 (IA leaf n15; front masthead leaf n0: ''APRIL 23, 1898'')", "verbatim_quote": "SHOW GOODS. Canvas, Poles, Stakes, Seats, Lights. Canvas made to order. A Line of Used Large and Small Tents. Fine Ballyhoo Umbrellas in bright colors up to eight feet across. Wire Hammocks that won''t rust. R. H. ARMBRUSTER, Springfield, Ill.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1898, "masthead_year": 1898, "linguistic_note": "Tentmaker R. H. Armbruster manufactures dedicated 8-foot brightly colored ''Ballyhoo Umbrellas'' shading the outside lecturer/ballyhoo stand, proving institutionalization of ''ballyhoo'' in American tent-and-awning trade catalogs by spring 1898.", "analysis_notes": "Verified display ad by Springfield, Ill. tent manufacturer R. H. Armbruster on p. 134. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-108.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1898 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-110', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'Ballyhoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1898, '1898-10-06', 'https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_1898-10-06_50_50/page/n9/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-110.webp', 127536, '282c5ba5f525859dcb3907ff01be24188ae7bdcb8cce17402e4d382ea5d14662', '{"id": "CERT-1800-110", "slug": "cert-1800-110", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "Ballyhoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1898, "date_display": "6 Oct 1898", "sort_date": "1898-10-06", "short_gloss": "Ballyhoo in St. Louis Post-Dispatch, Vol. 50, No. 50 (St. Louis, MO, Oct. 6, 1898)", "source_publication": "St. Louis Post-Dispatch, Vol. 50, No. 50 (St. Louis, MO, Oct. 6, 1898)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_1898-10-06_50_50/page/n9/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 50, No. 50, p. 10, col. 1 (''Big Thursday at the Fair''; IA leaf n9; masthead leaf n0: ''OCTOBER 6, 1898'')", "verbatim_quote": "The number of side shows on the grounds has increased two fold, and the voice of the \"Ballyhoo\" is heard in the land. Don''t know what a Ballyhoo is? Well, \"Ballyhoo\" is the latest vernacular for the gentleman who stands outside the tent and extols the merit of the show inside. He used to be called a \"Banker,\" [sic, for \"Barker,\"] but he''s a \"Ballyhoo\" this year.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1898, "masthead_year": 1898, "linguistic_note": "Pinpoints the exact Stage (a) -> Stage (b) metonymic shift in autumn 1898 (''\"Ballyhoo\" is the latest vernacular for the gentleman who stands outside the tent... He used to be called a \"B[ar]ker,\" but he''s a \"Ballyhoo\" this year''), 70 days earlier than OED3''s Dec. 15, 1898 citation in the same newspaper.", "analysis_notes": "Verified on Oct. 6, 1898 St. Louis Fair report, p. 10, col. 1. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-110.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1898 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-111', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'BALLYHOO MAN', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1898, '1898-12-10', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1898-12-10_46_41/page/n13/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-111.webp', 152248, 'd46c8bde079370750a6d2db7aae1deedad45a9d29c0038e19cfafaed94ed573d', '{"id": "CERT-1800-111", "slug": "cert-1800-111", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "BALLYHOO MAN", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1898, "date_display": "10 Dec 1898", "sort_date": "1898-12-10", "short_gloss": "BALLYHOO MAN in The New York Clipper, Vol. 46, No. 41 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Dec. 10, 1898)", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper, Vol. 46, No. 41 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Dec. 10, 1898)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1898-12-10_46_41/page/n13/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 46, No. 41, p. 700, col. 4 (IA leaf n13; front masthead leaf n0: ''DECEMBER 10, 1898'')", "verbatim_quote": "WANTED, FOR A STORE SHOW, SKETCH TEAM that can Sing and Dance; also one good BLACK FACE COMEDIAN and BALLYHOO MAN. Opened Dec. 15. 4 weeks work to good people. Address, full particulars, W. PULLARD, Care of Washington House, Norfolk, Va.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1898, "masthead_year": 1898, "linguistic_note": "Earliest verified attestation of the agent compound ''BALLYHOO MAN'' (recruited for a Norfolk, Va. winter ''STORE SHOW'' alongside a ''BLACK FACE COMEDIAN''), 15 years before Etymonline''s 1913 baseline for ''ballyhoo man''.", "analysis_notes": "Verified on Dec. 10, 1898 Clipper p. 700 classified notice. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-111.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1898 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-109', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'ballahoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1899, '1899-12-30', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1899-12-30_47_44/page/n12/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-109.webp', 178498, '167eaae14185e03636cbf1d8f07c65a2e1dc6199a8e4583478c0f1b22bdc3c39', '{"id": "CERT-1800-109", "slug": "cert-1800-109", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "ballahoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1899, "date_display": "30 Dec 1899", "sort_date": "1899-12-30", "short_gloss": "ballahoo in The New York Clipper, Vol. 47, No. 44 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Dec. 30, 1899)", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper, Vol. 47, No. 44 (New York: Frank Queen Pub. Co., Dec. 30, 1899)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1899-12-30_47_44/page/n12/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 47, No. 44, p. 925, col. 1 (IA leaf n12; front masthead leaf n0: ''DECEMBER 30, 1899'')", "verbatim_quote": "NOTES FROM BILLIE HAMMOND''S MIDWAY CARNIVAL SHOW.—... Old Bruin pulled the pole over to the table and cleaned out the cook house and then started down the Midway, carrying the pole with him. ... He took his stand in front of the ballahoo stage and remained there until his keeper came.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1899, "masthead_year": 1899, "linguistic_note": "Crucial orthographic bridge: spells midway ''ballyhoo'' as ''ballahoo'' (''ballahoo stage''; cf. Sept. 30, 1899 Clipper leaf n16 ''BALLAHOO PEOPLE... for my Midway Shows''), matching the exact traditional spelling of nautical ''ballahoo / ballyhoo'' (OED ballyhoo, n.1, 1836).", "analysis_notes": "Verified in Billie Hammond''s Midway Carnival Show dispatch from Dallas/San Antonio, p. 925. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-109.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1899 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-114', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'bally-hoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1900, '1900-12-08', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1900-12-08_12_32/page/n9/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-114.webp', 75178, 'e33d98ade9cf91e4bb5bce9884895355135729e23309d2fd45ba831ecf925b19', '{"id": "CERT-1800-114", "slug": "cert-1800-114", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "bally-hoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1900, "date_display": "8 Dec 1900", "sort_date": "1900-12-08", "short_gloss": "bally-hoo in The Billboard, Vol. 12, No. 32 (Cincinnati: Billboard Pub. Co., Dec. 8, 1900)", "source_publication": "The Billboard, Vol. 12, No. 32 (Cincinnati: Billboard Pub. Co., Dec. 8, 1900)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1900-12-08_12_32/page/n9/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 12, No. 32, p. 10, col. 2 (IA leaf n9; front masthead leaf n0: ''CINCINNATI, SATURDAY, DECEMBER 8, 1900'')", "verbatim_quote": "Francis Ferrari discharged the regular trainer (who had charge of Fatima, the \"coochee-cooche\" bear) at Columbus, Ga. All went well till they brought her out to \"bally-hoo\" the crowd at Savannah. The band played \"She Never Saw the Streets of Cairo\"...", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1900, "masthead_year": 1900, "linguistic_note": "Earliest verified verbal infinitive (''brought her out to \"bally-hoo\" the crowd at Savannah'' while the carnival band played ''Streets of Cairo'' outside Francis Ferari''s show), proving denominal conversion of Stage (a) platform performance into a transitive verb by Dec. 1900.", "analysis_notes": "Earliest hit in The Billboard (0 hits Nov. 1894-Nov. 1900); verified on Dec. 8, 1900 masthead and p. 10. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-114.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1900 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-204', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'Ballyhooley', 'hypothesis', 'supporting_pathway', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/IrishCome-all-yes/page/n80/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-204.webp', 78012, '7877cd64587f91807cfcc33d8e143bcaead0af65f226fda07f7561aeeb6514b8', '{"id": "CERT-1800-204", "slug": "cert-1800-204", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "Ballyhooley", "record_type": "hypothesis", "record_subtype": "supporting_pathway", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "1901", "sort_date": "1901-01-01", "short_gloss": "Linguistic comparison: Ballyhooley (1901)", "source_publication": "Manus O''Conor, Irish Com-All-Ye''s: A Repository of Ancient Irish Songs and Ballads (New York: The Popular Publishing Company, 1901), p. 73", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/IrishCome-all-yes/page/n80/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 73, col. 2 (IA leaf n80)", "verbatim_quote": "BALLYHOOLEY. THERE''S a dashing sort of boy, who is called his mother''s joy, / His ructions and his elements they charm me; / He takes the chief command in a water-drinking band, / Called the Ballyhooley Blue Ribbon Army. ... CHORUS. Willoo loo! hoo! hoo! we will all enlist, you know, / For their principles and elements they charm me; / Sure they don''t care what they ate, if they drink their whisky nate, / In the Ballyhooley Blue Ribbon Army.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "R. J. Martin''s ''Ballyhooly'' (1886) -> secondary musical/walkaround reinforcer for US carnival ballyhoo (PLWK vs. PLWKLW = )", "analysis_notes": "Full American songster printing of Martin''s ''Ballyhooley'' (''chief command in a water-drinking band, Called the Ballyhooley Blue Ribbon Army; Chorus: Willoo loo! hoo! hoo!''). Phonological contact score(''ballyhoo'',''Ballyhooly'',1886,1901) yields (chronology_plausible=True vs. 1901 midway ballyhoo), supporting secondary acoustic/band reinforcement in 1888-1899 US variety, while pre-1886 US ''THE GRAND BALLYHOO'' (1877) and ''ballahoo'' clamor (1884) rule it out as sole root.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-204.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-115', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'ballyhoo', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-03-02', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1901-03-02_13_9/page/n4/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-115.webp', 99926, '3bc61c8dd402a7f2c02a46a05d3ab8834dacac5401ca7b3d1c2f6a573af5b665', '{"id": "CERT-1800-115", "slug": "cert-1800-115", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "ballyhoo", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "2 Mar 1901", "sort_date": "1901-03-02", "short_gloss": "ballyhoo in The Billboard, Vol. 13, No. 9 (Cincinnati: Billboard Pub. Co., Mar. 2, 1901)", "source_publication": "The Billboard, Vol. 13, No. 9 (Cincinnati: Billboard Pub. Co., Mar. 2, 1901)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1901-03-02_13_9/page/n4/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 13, No. 9, p. 5, col. 2 (IA leaf n4; front masthead leaf n0: ''MARCH 2, 1901'')", "verbatim_quote": "It was this affliction of the muscles, Mr. Worrall intimates, that led him from the bar of the State to the ballyhoo of the circus. In conclusion, he asks his fellow showman in Kokomo to seek out the spot where rest his mortal parts...", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Earliest unquoted lowercase noun attestation in The Billboard, showing ''the ballyhoo of the circus'' already treated as the emblematic institution of tented circus life five months before Hartt''s Aug. 1901 World''s Work article.", "analysis_notes": "Verified on Mar. 2, 1901 masthead and p. 5 showman eulogy. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-115.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-116', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'ballyhoo-ing', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-04-20', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1901-04-20_13_16/page/n11/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-116.webp', 111796, '9d118d409b44dc2e4059369647b710213782a6676b59d37244674580122d79a1', '{"id": "CERT-1800-116", "slug": "cert-1800-116", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "ballyhoo-ing", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "20 Apr 1901", "sort_date": "1901-04-20", "short_gloss": "ballyhoo-ing in The Billboard, Vol. 13, No. 16 (Cincinnati: Billboard Pub. Co., Apr. 20, 1901)", "source_publication": "The Billboard, Vol. 13, No. 16 (Cincinnati: Billboard Pub. Co., Apr. 20, 1901)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1901-04-20_13_16/page/n11/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 13, No. 16, p. 12, col. 3 (IA leaf n11; front masthead leaf n0: ''APRIL 20, 1901'')", "verbatim_quote": "Toward the close of the season De Funiak Springs was turned into a regular \"midway\"—H. E. Murray''s merry-go-round, Gill''s Australian Circus, the Electrical Palace of Amusements, Anderson''s Steam Riding Gallery and Speyer''s Wild West all competing for honors, with two to three bands \"ballyhoo- ing\" the streets all the time.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Documents brass bands ''\"ballyhoo-ing\" the streets all the time'' on an improvised Florida winter ''midway'', antedating OED ''ballyhooing'' (1902), Green''s ''ballyhooing'' (Nov. 4, 1903), and OED ''ballyhoo, v.'' (1911).", "analysis_notes": "Line-break hyphen ''ballyhoo-\\n ing'' verified directly in physical lead type on p. 12, col. 3. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-116.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-112', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'ballyhoos', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-06-28', 'https://panewsarchive.psu.edu/lccn/sn84026355/1901-06-28/ed-1/seq-4/', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-112.webp', 155002, '1ac3319aba003ce5ddb4d93c260081ade27f795e10802618822900f47ff0094d', '{"id": "CERT-1800-112", "slug": "cert-1800-112", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "ballyhoos", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "28 Jun 1901", "sort_date": "1901-06-28", "short_gloss": "ballyhoos in The Scranton Tribune (Scranton, PA), June 28, 1901, ''Some of the Scenes on Buffalo''s Midway''", "source_publication": "The Scranton Tribune (Scranton, PA), June 28, 1901, ''Some of the Scenes on Buffalo''s Midway''", "source_archive": "Pennsylvania Newspaper Archive (Penn State / Open-ONI)", "source_url": "https://panewsarchive.psu.edu/lccn/sn84026355/1901-06-28/ed-1/seq-4/", "page_and_column": "p. 4, col. 2 (seq-4; front masthead seq-1: ''SCRANTON, PA., FRIDAY MORNING, JUNE 28, 1901'')", "verbatim_quote": "However that may be, what it lacks in so-called spice is made up in an inferno of racket kept going by the \"ballyhoos\" outside the doors. Now a \"ballyhoo\" is an individual who is employed for lung qualities alone. ... The \"bally-hoo\" outside Bostock''s arena is a gigantic young man with a voice in proportion.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Shows how the 1901 Buffalo Pan-American Exposition Midway popularized ''ballyhoo'' nationwide to general newspaper readers (who still needed it glossed in scare quotes two months before Hartt''s Aug. 1901 World''s Work article).", "analysis_notes": "Verified on June 28, 1901 Scranton Tribune masthead and p. 4 Buffalo Midway dispatch. .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-112.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1800-113', 'TGT-033', 'ballyhoo', NULL, 'ballyhoo / ballahoo', 'ballyhooer', 'attestation', 'prior_art_baseline', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-08-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_worlds-work_1901-08_2_4/page/n89/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-113.webp', 63564, '34a7082c93592354ad8a7c07ebc6a0c6f893f5ff47feb0cc8edd714dcb7ef745', '{"id": "CERT-1800-113", "slug": "cert-1800-113", "case_slug": "ballyhoo", "headword": "ballyhoo / ballahoo", "attested_form": "ballyhooer", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "prior_art_baseline", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "Aug 1901", "sort_date": "1901-08-01", "short_gloss": "ballyhooer in Mary Bronson Hartt, ''The Play-Side of the Fair,'' The World''s Work, Vol. 2, No. 4 (New York: Doubleday, Page & Co., Aug. 1901)", "source_publication": "Mary Bronson Hartt, ''The Play-Side of the Fair,'' The World''s Work, Vol. 2, No. 4 (New York: Doubleday, Page & Co., Aug. 1901)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_worlds-work_1901-08_2_4/page/n89/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 2, No. 4, p. 1100, col. 2 (IA leaf n89; issue title leaf n4: ''AUGUST, 1901 — VOLUME II, NUMBER 4'')", "verbatim_quote": "Last of the professions on the Midway are those of the \"barker,\" \"ballyhooer\" and \"spieler.\" Step into the Midway on any warm night from out the silent glow of the great illuminated courts, and you will hear this profession at work.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Canonical Aug. 1901 baseline in OED (''ballyhooer, n.''), OED2, HDAS, Green''s, and Etymonline; also exposes a Trap A Google Books bound-volume misdate (''1900'' on worldswork11pagegoog for Vol. II, May-Oct. 1901).", "analysis_notes": "Verified on Aug. 1901 issue imprint (leaf n4) and p. 1100 (leaf n89). .", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-113.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
