15, 1905) catches the exact moment US carnival noun ''bally'' (''Gail Alden will handle the announcement on the bally'', p. 20) emerges in free variation alongside unclipped ''Singers for Bally-hoo'' / ''The greatest ballyhoo you can own'' (p. 34) and ''Strong Bally hoo'' (p. 40), proving reverse derivation (ballyhoo [1901] -> bally [1905]).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/ballyhoo/CERT-1800-212.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1905 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026. WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
