plicitly credited to Merriam-Webster, illustrating Missouri down-river press diffusion 16 days after Booster O''Reilly''s Oct. 12, 1904 St. Louis Post-Dispatch confession (''the latest discovery in the criminology catalogue'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": null, "rights_status": "external_archive_link", "rights_note": "Published 1904 (<= 1930): inspect original scan via host archive URL."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-118', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'grafters', 'rejected_lead', 'ocr_ink_ghost_for_grafters', 'agent_verified', 1905, '1905-10-05', 'https://archive.org/details/rhinelander-new-north-1905-10-05/page/n0/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-118.webp', 194482, '4e206dde881f3080a50fcb8aa65549f9f727717a54983af55fc848b508d15980', '{"id": "CERT-2100-118", "slug": "cert-2100-118", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "grafters", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "ocr_ink_ghost_for_grafters", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1905, "date_display": "5 Oct 1905", "sort_date": "1905-10-05", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: grafters", "source_publication": "The New North (Rhinelander, WI)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (rhinelander-new-north-1905-10-05)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/rhinelander-new-north-1905-10-05/page/n0/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 1, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "The first day he had 18 straight shaves at 15 cents each, and that evening the manager discharged him, saying: \"We want grafters here.\" A barber, he said, who couldn''t \"cop out\" a half dozen hair cuts and shampoos from 18 shaves, whether needed or not, was \"no good.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1905, "linguistic_note": "Falsified Trap B bi-tonal scan OCR ghost: J. P. Johnston''s syndicated ''Stories of the Fakirs'' prints ''grafters'' (matching ''THE BARBER SHOP GRAFT'' subhead), not ''grifters''.", "analysis_notes": "Critical 1905 Trap B falsification: J. P. Johnston''s syndicated con-man feature ''Stories of the Fakirs'' (copyright 1905 by Joseph B. Bowles) produced dirty-OCR hits for ''grifters'' (Oct. 5, 1905) and ''grifter'' (Oct. 19, 1905) in Rhinelander New North, alongside 1905-06-09 Dakota Farmers'' Leader and 1905-10-25 NYT p. 8. Multimodal inspection of all four 1905 scans proves every one prints ''grafter(s)'' in physical ink.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-118.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1905 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-119', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'Grift', 'attestation', 'earliest_circus_trade_press_grift_noun', 'agent_verified', 1906, '1906-06-16', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1906-06-16_18_24/page/n52/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-119.webp', 115964, '195574ee83f0d666a0f17e60913618866d1e372e0e89f245f643c6425ba8e36b', '{"id": "CERT-2100-119", "slug": "cert-2100-119", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "Grift", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "earliest_circus_trade_press_grift_noun", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1906, "date_display": "16 Jun 1906", "sort_date": "1906-06-16", "short_gloss": "Grift in The Billboard (Cincinnati, OH)", "source_publication": "The Billboard (Cincinnati, OH)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_billboard_1906-06-16_18_24)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1906-06-16_18_24/page/n52/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 18, No. 24, p. 54, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "WANTED — Merry-go-round, Shows, Concessions and Grift for Eagles'' Big Picnic, near here, July 4th. Four Special Chartered Trains; 8,000 people. Also want open time of all free attraction performers; am booking circuit of Fairs Parks and Reunions. Roy Chance, Jack Cavanaugh, write. Shows will get big money here. Address FRED M. CLANCY, Mgr. Cassel & Clancy Booking Agency, Room 7, First Nat''l Bank Bldg., Ft. Smith, Ark.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1906, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "NOVEL SHOWBIZ TRADE-PRESS BREAKTHROUGH — Earliest primary-scan-verified occurrence of ''grift, n.2'' in The Billboard or any theatrical/midway trade periodical (June 16, 1906, -8 years vs OED & GDoS 1914 ''grift, n.2''). Running header (''54 The Billboard JUNE 16, 1906.'') and 4x ink macro verify unquoted trade-classified solicitation of ''Merry-go-round, Shows, Concessions and Grift'' by Ft. Smith, AR carnival booking agent Fred M. Clancy.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-119.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1906 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-120', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'Grift', 'contextual_evidence', 'josiah_flynt_diachronic_shift_proof', 'agent_verified', 1907, '1907-02-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_cosmopolitan_1907-02_42_4/page/n1/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-120.webp', 51700, '38f0e4af29004d7bc15c4b6fe2c1dac7fdebaeb9e1290c669c4becd5f10aa941', '{"id": "CERT-2100-120", "slug": "cert-2100-120", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "Grift", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "josiah_flynt_diachronic_shift_proof", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1907, "date_display": "1 Feb 1907", "sort_date": "1907-02-01", "short_gloss": "Grift in Cosmopolitan Magazine (New York, NY) [Josiah Flynt, ''The Pool-Room Vampire'']", "source_publication": "Cosmopolitan Magazine (New York, NY) [Josiah Flynt, ''The Pool-Room Vampire'']", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_cosmopolitan_1907-02_42_4)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_cosmopolitan_1907-02_42_4/page/n1/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 42, No. 4, pp. 359, 363 [leaves 1, 4, 11]", "verbatim_quote": "On starting my investigation, the first thing that arrested my attention was a word of four letters—D-O-P-E. This word is as puzzling as the word Graft. The professional criminal seldom uses the word Graft. He says Grift.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1907, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "Decisive diachronic bookend (-7 years vs OED/GDoS 1914 ''grift, n.2''): Josiah Flynt (Josiah Flynt Willard, d. Jan. 20, 1907; text composed late 1906) had used ''graft''/''grafter'' exclusively with 0 ''grift*'' tokens in The Powers That Prey (1900) and The World of Graft (1901). By late 1906 / Feb. 1907 (and Apr. 1907 Cosmopolitan p. 676: ''one particular Grift—the gambling and sure-thing privileges at fairs'' and ''First Ward Grifter''), Flynt explicitly reports that professional criminals had abandoned ''Graft'' for ''Grift''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-120.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1907 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-209', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'Grift', 'attestation', 'derivative_antedating', 'agent_verified', 1907, '1907-04-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_cosmopolitan_1907-04_42_6', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-209.webp', 85774, 'ebbfce13f8daf2ce7dff7f055ad592a02a5b756913ee5594c3384633a00f0873', '{"id": "CERT-2100-209", "slug": "cert-2100-209", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "Grift", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "derivative_antedating", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1907, "date_display": "Apr 1907", "sort_date": "1907-04-01", "short_gloss": "Grift in Josiah Flynt, ''The Pool-Room Vampire,'' Cosmopolitan Magazine, Vol. 42, No. 6 (April 1907), p. 641 [leaf 48]", "source_publication": "Josiah Flynt, ''The Pool-Room Vampire,'' Cosmopolitan Magazine, Vol. 42, No. 6 (April 1907), p. 641 [leaf 48]", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_cosmopolitan_1907-04_42_6", "page_and_column": "", "verbatim_quote": "\"Big Tim\" Sullivan, congressman, race-horse owner, saloon proprietor, and valuable factor in Tammany, stands out as the most scandalous individual in the pool-room Grift in the United States.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1907, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Intra-authorial smoking gun: after 0 hits across all 1899-1902 books, Josiah Flynt himself adopts ''the pool-room Grift'', ''systematizing the Grift'', and ''grifter'' (p. 644, naming Big Tim Sullivan, Mont Tennes, Charles Smith, and Harry Perry) just before his Jan. 1907 death (-7y vs. OED 1914 grift, n.2).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-209.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1907 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-121', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'grift', 'attestation', 'circus_proprietor_daily_grift_split', 'agent_verified', 1907, '1907-04-20', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1907-04-20_19_16/page/n30/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-121.webp', 93002, '0cd1f61b9e651ca75daa91c59c815df62544e9747f09229506f57c7fadd3ab79', '{"id": "CERT-2100-121", "slug": "cert-2100-121", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "grift", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "circus_proprietor_daily_grift_split", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1907, "date_display": "20 Apr 1907", "sort_date": "1907-04-20", "short_gloss": "grift in The Billboard (Cincinnati, OH)", "source_publication": "The Billboard (Cincinnati, OH)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_billboard_1907-04-20_19_16)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1907-04-20_19_16/page/n30/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 19, No. 16, p. 31 [leaf 31], col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "But of all the characters the one seemingly lost to the hardship of the trip was \"Hungry.\" The show when it started was in for the \"grift.\" Jerry split it up daily with the proprietor of the circus and he had a hard time in getting anything to make a split.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1907, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "Primary-scan-verified circus institutional attestation in The Billboard (-7 years vs OED & GDoS 1914 ''grift, n.2''), documenting a grift-carrying tent circus (''was in for the \"grift\"'') whose privilege boss (''Jerry'') split daily swindle proceeds with the circus proprietor.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-121.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1907 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-122', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'grifting', 'contextual_evidence', 'circus_lexical_bleaching_replacement_testimony', 'agent_verified', 1907, '1907-06-10', 'https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn92051126/1907-06-10/ed-1/?sp=9', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-122.webp', 172182, '58c6501694211fa47bdb935205bbc18180079b021dc574b7900bd7c22a2ea808', '{"id": "CERT-2100-122", "slug": "cert-2100-122", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "grifting", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "circus_lexical_bleaching_replacement_testimony", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1907, "date_display": "10 Jun 1907", "sort_date": "1907-06-10", "short_gloss": "grifting in The New Haven Union (New Haven, CT)", "source_publication": "The New Haven Union (New Haven, CT)", "source_archive": "Library of Congress Chronicling America (LCCN sn92051126)", "source_url": "https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn92051126/1907-06-10/ed-1/?sp=9", "page_and_column": "p. 9, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "\"''Grafting George'' is the name applied to any of the gambling fraternity that may be about. And, by the way, do you happen to know that the circus man has dropped the expression ''grafting'' to a considerable extent? I guess it became too common and so was eliminated from the circus man''s vocabulary. It''s now ''grifting,'' if you would be considered ''up'' in the language of the tented show.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1907, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "Smoking-gun sociolinguistic explanation of the graft -> grift vowel shift (-8 years vs OED & GDoS 1915 ''grifting, vbl. n.''): an interviewed circus insider explains that once ''grafting'' became too common in general public speech (post-1901 municipal muckraking), circus showmen deliberately eliminated it in favor of ''grifting'' as esoteric ''language of the tented show'' alongside ''clem'' and ''Hey, Rube''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-122.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1907 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-210', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'Grafter', 'contextual_evidence', 'negative_corpus_boundary', 'agent_verified', 1908, '1908-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/gentlegrafterhen00henrrich', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-210.webp', 61162, '5b8018549d93fae20725f6ac6fbbf87cd955aedab097b05dc6d3ea4f5fb777a3', '{"id": "CERT-2100-210", "slug": "cert-2100-210", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "Grafter", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "negative_corpus_boundary", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1908, "date_display": "1908", "sort_date": "1908-01-01", "short_gloss": "Grafter in O. Henry [William Sydney Porter], The Gentle Grafter (New York: The McClure Company, 1908), Title & Copyright", "source_publication": "O. Henry [William Sydney Porter], The Gentle Grafter (New York: The McClure Company, 1908), Title & Copyright", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/gentlegrafterhen00henrrich", "page_and_column": "", "verbatim_quote": "Copyright, 1908, by The McClure Company. [Title: The Gentle Grafter, by O. Henry — 153x graft/grafter, 0x grift/grifter across entire 1908 text]", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1908, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Explains why O. Henry titled his 1908 con-man collection The Gentle Grafter (153x graft*, 0x grift*): Porter acquired his underworld vocabulary in the Ohio Penitentiary (1898-1901) prior to the c. 1902-1904 grift split, matching Hapgood 1903 (326x/0x), No. 1500 Sing Sing 1904 (0x), Wooldridge 1906 (54x/0x), and Will Irwin 1909 (50x/0x).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-210.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1908 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-123', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'the grift', 'attestation', 'collective_noun_the_grift_antedating', 'agent_verified', 1909, '1909-06-03', 'https://archive.org/details/rushville-daily-republican-1909-06-03/page/n7/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-123.webp', 76534, '68647897d1a81ab1963b589fa5ca8acf7a2f0607ee0aff0ebbf1354d3888568d', '{"id": "CERT-2100-123", "slug": "cert-2100-123", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "the grift", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "collective_noun_the_grift_antedating", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1909, "date_display": "3 Jun 1909", "sort_date": "1909-06-03", "short_gloss": "the grift in The Daily Republican (Rushville, IN)", "source_publication": "The Daily Republican (Rushville, IN)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (rushville-daily-republican-1909-06-03)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/rushville-daily-republican-1909-06-03/page/n7/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 6, No. 70, pp. 7–8, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "It''s like this pal. I''m out with the big trick. Working with the grift. [...] The bulls swept down on the grift and I had just lit a brain tablet when one of ''em blowed up and asked where he could find the main squeeze.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1909, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "Antedates OED grift, n.2 (1914) by 5 years and Green''s collective sense ''the grift'' (1923, Hammett) by 14 years. Uses ''the grift'' twice across pp. 7–8 (''Working with the grift'' alongside ''the big trick'' [= railroad circus] and ''The bulls swept down on the grift''), illustrating both collective circus-midway usage and an early V + on + [the grift] syntactic bridge.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-123.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1909 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-124', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'grifting', 'attestation', 'earliest_verified_participial_adjective_grifting', 'agent_verified', 1909, '1909-06-12', 'https://archive.org/details/ShowWorldv4n25/page/n7/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-124.webp', 70520, 'c6ed2258a1182a7dbc93617d99af2cabce67c342ddf9c8fe22423a6431e2950e', '{"id": "CERT-2100-124", "slug": "cert-2100-124", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "grifting", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "earliest_verified_participial_adjective_grifting", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1909, "date_display": "12 Jun 1909", "sort_date": "1909-06-12", "short_gloss": "grifting in The Show World (Chicago, IL)", "source_publication": "The Show World (Chicago, IL)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (ShowWorldv4n25)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/ShowWorldv4n25/page/n7/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 4, No. 25, p. 8 [leaf 8], col. 1", "verbatim_quote": "The circus season of 1909 promises to prove one of the most profitable in a decade. The reports which reach this office indicate that the majority of the tent shows are doing well, with the possible exception of \"grifting outfits\" and the small shows now in the south.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1909, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "Earliest primary-scan-verified attributive participial adjective ''grifting'' (''\"grifting outfits\"'') in a circus/theatrical trade journal, found via systematic 156-issue sweep of Warren A. Patrick''s Chicago trade weekly The Show World (1907-1911); antedates OED/GDoS 1915 ''grifting'' benchmarks by 6 years.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-124.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1909 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-125', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'grifters', 'attestation', 'mainstream_magazine_circus_jargon_gloss', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-05-14', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n15/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-125.webp', 68040, 'dcd703d299d8079e35261674fe40c18471c872a36020e66de640dffb005eaf26', '{"id": "CERT-2100-125", "slug": "cert-2100-125", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "grifters", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "mainstream_magazine_circus_jargon_gloss", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "14 May 1910", "sort_date": "1910-05-14", "short_gloss": "grifters in The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia, PA)", "source_publication": "The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia, PA)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n15/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 182, No. 46, pp. 15-16, 48 [leaves 15-16, 48]", "verbatim_quote": "\"It was comin'' to Sellers,\" growled the Colonel. \"He''s been carryin'' too strong a crowd of grifters with him; three-card workers and strong-arm men and stick-ups and the like, and they was bound to put him on the blink some day.\" [...] The two men with him, and also a couple of \"grifters\"—circus jargon for small swindlers, short-change men and the like—paused to watch.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "Antedates OED grifter, n. (1915) by 5 years and Green''s Dictionary of Slang (1911, Mathews) by 1 year. George Randolph Chester''s Saturday Evening Post circus story ''Ballyhoo Bill'' explicitly glosses ''\"grifters\"—circus jargon for small swindlers, short-change men, and the like'' alongside ''shillabers'' and ''three-card workers''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-125.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-126', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'drifted', 'rejected_lead', 'ocr_ink_ghost_for_drifted', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-09-17', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1910-09-17_58_31/page/n4/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-126.webp', 65240, '593e28615ad89054fd9057d39d9a1b65129a3728dbe9182faef3c8bd70ebc824', '{"id": "CERT-2100-126", "slug": "cert-2100-126", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "drifted", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "ocr_ink_ghost_for_drifted", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "17 Sep 1910", "sort_date": "1910-09-17", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: drifted", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1910-09-17_58_31)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1910-09-17_58_31/page/n4/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 58, No. 31, p. 764 [leaf 4], col. 4", "verbatim_quote": "TOM NORTH''S VISIT. Tom North, of the Gentry Circus, drifted into Cincinnati to enjoy the Ohio Valley Exposition before he resumes his position as business manager of \"The Newlyweds.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Falsified Trap B OCR ghost: physical ink prints ''drifted into Cincinnati'', misread by IA OCR as ''Grifted Into Cincinnatt''.", "analysis_notes": "Instructive circus trade-press Trap B audit across The New York Clipper: all four pre-1914 Clipper OCR hits for grift-family lemmas proved on scan inspection to be OCR ghosts or homographs—1902-09-27 ''Vander-grift, Pa.'' (Trap C), 1908-06-27 ''\"The Lady Grafter''s Reception\"'' (OCR ''Grifters''), 1909-01-23 ''Die Kralle (La Griffe)'' (OCR ''1a Grifter''), 1910-09-17 ''drifted'' (OCR ''Grifted''), and 1913-12-20 ''paying the \"graft.\"'' (OCR ''grift'')—showing that conservative New York Clipper copy-editors resisted circus midway ''grift'' longer than Cincinnati-based The Billboard.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-126.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2100-127', 'TGT-100', 'grifter', NULL, 'grifter', 'Grifter', 'contextual_evidence', 'variety_vaudeville_coin_manipulator_charactonym', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-10-08', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_variety_1910-10-08_20_5/page/n9/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-127.webp', 58222, 'e9a741030790b37f07f0065d6cdb96705a9b8163476ef01dc9df98652708cace', '{"id": "CERT-2100-127", "slug": "cert-2100-127", "case_slug": "grifter", "headword": "grifter", "attested_form": "Grifter", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "variety_vaudeville_coin_manipulator_charactonym", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "8 Oct 1910", "sort_date": "1910-10-08", "short_gloss": "Grifter in Variety (New York, NY)", "source_publication": "Variety (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_variety_1910-10-08_20_5)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_variety_1910-10-08_20_5/page/n9/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 20, No. 5, p. 10 [leaf 10], col. 3", "verbatim_quote": "East Cranberry, O., Oct. Dear Mike: There was a couple of fellers named Grifter and Gitney that wrote to me and said if I would put them in with my show bookings for one week they would perform their coin manipulating act for A. K.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Deliberate American underworld, railroad-depot, and circus-midway cant vowel-ablaut / blend alteration of grafter, n. (''corrupt official or swindler'', 1865) + graft, n., reinforced by midway drifter / shift among traveling ''sure-thing'' flat-joint and privilege operators c. 1900-1904 as ''graft/grafter'' bleached into mainstream municipal politics.", "analysis_notes": "Earliest verified Variety trade-paper deployment (-5 years vs OED 1915): J. H. Murphy (of Murphy and Willard) coins the comic vaudeville team name ''Grifter and Gitney'' (pairing ''grifter'' = short-change swindler + ''gitney/jitney'' = five-cent coin) for a ''coin manipulating act'', proving vaudeville trade readers immediately recognized the short-change coin-swindle sense of ''grifter'' by Oct. 1910.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/grifter/CERT-2100-127.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
