ury agricultural/plantation manuals ''hoe-boy'' has 0 hits (''hoe-hand'' and ''hoe-gang'' are standard). In newspapers it surfaces only as an ad-hoc Southern mission schoolboy label (1818 Reflector p. 2) or comic pun on musical hautboy (''For the farmer, the hoe boy'', 1885 Sunny South p. 5), with 0 hits in 1870s–1888 Pacific Northwest/Idaho/Montana rail corridors.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-311.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1818 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
