obes... Barege Robes'' misread as ''Hobos''; (2) 1865 insurance notice ''It is a HOME COMPANY'' misread as ''HOBOI COMPANY''; (3) 1873 Sapolio soap ad ''ENOCH MORGAN''S SONS'' misread as ''ENOCH HOBO''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-320.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1858 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2300-321', 'TGT-066', 'hobo', NULL, 'hobo', 'nightman', 'rejected_lead', 'homograph_false_friend', 'agent_verified', 1859, '1859-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/dictionaryofamer00bartiala/page/n234/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-321.webp', 53924, '697468b879572e899ae98f7a30e20b543f5adf618ddc415ad958fca75cfc35fc', '{"id": "CERT-2300-321", "slug": "cert-2300-321", "case_slug": "hobo", "headword": "hobo", "attested_form": "nightman", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "homograph_false_friend", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1859, "date_display": "1859", "sort_date": "1859-01-01", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: nightman", "source_publication": "John Russell Bartlett, Dictionary of Americanisms, 2nd ed. (Boston, 1859), p. 197 & 4th ed. (1884), p. 288; The Century Dictionary, Vol. IV (1904), p. 2848", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/dictionaryofamer00bartiala/page/n234/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Bartlett 1859 p. 197 (n234); Bartlett 1884 p. 288 (n341); Century IV p. 2848 col. 3 (n189)", "verbatim_quote": "ies. Ho-Boy or Haut-Boy. A nightman. New York. The Thames, below London, is odorous with t", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1859, "linguistic_note": "Trap C Red-Team Falsification #1: Early ''hoboy''/''hoboe'' (< Fr. hautbois ''oboe'') & NY ''Ho-Boy'' (''nightman/night-scavenger'')", "analysis_notes": "Disentangles two major Trap C homographs: (1) 16th–19th-c. English hoboy/hoboe and Dutch hobo (''oboe'', < Fr. hautbois, kept strictly separate in Century Dict. 1904 p. 2848 & Standard Dict. 1893 p. 864); (2) New York slang ''Ho-Boy or Haut-Boy. A nightman'' (Bartlett 1859 p. 197, citing Scientific American Aug. 8, 1857; copied into Farmer 1889 p. 299), an ironic municipal euphemism playing on musical hautboy for nocturnal privy-cleaners (like Charleston ''hoboy'' watchman/oboe cries), semantically and geographically unrelated to 1888 PNW rail hobos (though later echoed in Roving Bill Aspinwall''s 1893 pun ''Haut Beaus'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-321.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1859 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
