and vags. Prosopographical merge (2300-B): Portland Police Captain Cardwell explains at the western terminus of the Northern Pacific and O.R.&N./Oregon Short Line how freight-riding vagrants repeated ''hobo'' outside closed boxcars as a fraternal countersign (''sesame'') to have the door drawn back.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-109.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1888 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
