t''. On p. 299 between HOBBLE-BUSH and HOCK, Farmer records solely ''HO-BOY or HAUT BOY. — A New York night scavenger'' (copied from Bartlett 1859/1877), as Josiah Flynt explicitly observed in 1899 (p. 394).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-305.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1889 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
