 from Laramie, Wyo. (dated Aug. 23, 1890) applauding North Platte UP shopman ''Hobo'' (July 24, 1890 letter) and naming UP Supt. of Machinery Harvey Middleton, Cheyenne K. of L. leader Thomas Neasham, General Foreman Hickey, Clerk Nash, Master Mechanic Mertzheimmer, and General Foreman Joseph Roberts (cf. also Vol. 7, Aug. 1892, unionpacificemp04corbgoog: UP mechanic ''TIM'' contrasting steady shops with itinerant boomer mechanics—\"Of course ''hobo''s'' drift in and out again... ''hobo'' service with ''hobo'' pay\").", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-213.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1890 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
