066 baseline trajectory: still absent in Maitland''s Chicago slang dictionary (1891, p. 142), hobo enters Funk & Wagnalls'' Standard Dictionary Vol. I (1893, p. 864: ''ho\\''bo [Western U. S.] An idle, shiftless, wandering workman, ranking scarcely above the tramp''), Dialect Notes I (1895, p. 389: ''Western (but well-nigh universal now)''), and Century Dictionary IV (1904, p. 2848: ''[Western U. S.]'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/hobo/CERT-2300-310.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1893 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
