on the South Wabash / Eldridge Court axis (two blocks east of 300 S. State St.) calling confidence steerers Schlepper; corroborated by Sept. 21, 1895 p. 1 (''geriebene Bauernfänger und „Schlepper“'') and July 12, 1895 p. 1.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-106.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1895 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-105', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Schlepper', 'hypothesis', 'supporting_pathway', 'agent_verified', 1897, '1897-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/encyklopdisches00muregoog/page/n629/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-105.webp', 183082, '3c00e2a4ceb1e7e49e2f6b8575d09bc3ed729700c5dc9e225d0b5b8ca2ab77e6', '{"id": "CERT-1400-105", "slug": "cert-1400-105", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Schlepper", "record_type": "hypothesis", "record_subtype": "supporting_pathway", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1897, "date_display": "1897", "sort_date": "1897-01-01", "short_gloss": "Bilingual lexicon equation: American ''roper-in'' = ''Lockvogel, Schlepper'' (Muret-Sanders c. 1897)", "source_publication": "Eduard Muret & Daniel Sanders, Encyklopädisches Wörterbuch, Teil I, Bd. 2 (Berlin & New York, c. 1897-1900), leaf n629; paired with Teil II, Bd. 2 (c. 1901), p. 1765 (leaf n611)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/encyklopdisches00muregoog/page/n629/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Teil I, Bd. 2, s.v. ''roper-in'' (IA leaf n629); Teil II, Bd. 2, p. 1765, s.v. ''Schlepper'' (leaf n611)", "verbatim_quote": "roper-in Am. (ro''p-er-i''n) s. 1. = roper 4. — 2. sl. Lockvogel m, Schlepper m.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1897, "linguistic_note": "Consonant-skeleton comparison against full-stem ''shillaber'' (SLPL): ''Schlepper'' (SLPL) matches all four consonant positions (edit distance 0; chronologically plausible: True).", "analysis_notes": "Direct Americanism bilingual equation: Muret-Sanders glosses American slang roper-in (the exact co-referent used alongside shillabers in 7 June 1883 Chicago Tribune ''roped-in and robbed'') as Lockvogel m, Schlepper m, while Teil II leaf n611 glosses Schlepper sense 2 as sl. bonneter, jackal; runner; tout(er). Leaf n748 lists Shillaber only as humorist B. P. Shillaber.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-105.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1897 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-311', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Shilling', 'rejected_lead', 'uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology', 'agent_verified', 1898, '1898-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/englishyiddishan00harkuoft/page/n806/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-311.webp', 140522, 'c9930aceb044ba23627a41f3594aeb49688cfb6f90fc8996fcb341fd4fe6d97e', '{"id": "CERT-1200-311", "slug": "cert-1200-311", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Shilling", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1898, "date_display": "1898", "sort_date": "1898-01-01", "short_gloss": "Rejected lead (uncorroborated or folk etymology)", "source_publication": "Alexander Harkavy, Yiddish-English Dictionary / יידיש-ענגלישער ווערטערבוך (New York: copyright 1898 by Alexander Harkavy; bound with English-Yiddish Dictionary, copyright 1891, in IA englishyiddishan00harkuoft), Yiddish-English p. 349, col. 2 (leaf n806, ''שילד''–''שימלען'') & English-Yiddish p. 563, cols. 1-2 (leaf n576, ''Shibboleth'' & ''Shiftless''–''Shin''); cross-checked in Harkavy''s 1925 Yiddish-English-Hebrew Dictionary (nybc201108)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/englishyiddishan00harkuoft/page/n806/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "1898 Copyright & Title leaves n1154-n1155; Yiddish-English p. 349 col. 2 (leaf n806); English-Yiddish p. 563 cols. 1-2 (leaf n576)", "verbatim_quote": "שילטען va. to curse, to execrate. שילינג m. 1) third part of a Polish groschen, doit, farthing ... 2) shilling (English money). שילינגער m. ז. שילינג. שילער m. scholar, pupil. שילערין f. female pupil. שימלען vn. to mould. ... [English-Yiddish p. 563: Shibboleth (שיב''באָלעטה) אַ פּראָבע-װאָרט ... Shiftless ... Shillaloh ז. Shillaly. Shillaly אַ גראָבער שטעקען. Shilling אַ שילינג ... Shilly-shally ... Shin]", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": null, "linguistic_note": "Viral internet/Wikipedia ghost etymology claiming English shill is ''an abbreviation of the Yiddish shillaber'' (plus online StackExchange folk etymology from Yiddish/Hebrew shibboleth ''watchword'') — FALSIFIED as a 100% nonexistent Yiddish ghost word.", "analysis_notes": "FALSIFIED-MYTH (1200-C Domain 3 Yiddish Ghost-Root Kill): An unsourced 2009 Wikipedia edit (''it may be an abbreviation of the Yiddish shillaber'') was mirrored across dozens of reference sites, flagged as a ''house of mirrors'' by Gabe Burns on Sesquiotica (25 Apr. 2011) and dismissed by Yiddish lexicographer David L. Gold (15 Apr. 2020: ''No Yidish lexeme or collocation of Yidish lexemes comes to mind that could be an immediate or a non-immediate etymon of English shill or English shillaber''). Our visual page-scan audit of Harkavy''s 1898 Yiddish-English Dictionary (p. 349 col. 2, leaf n806) provides hard photographic proof: the entire Yiddish שיל- (shil-) sequence consists solely of שילד (''shield, sign''), שילדערונג (''description''), שילדערן (''describe''), שילד-קרעט (''tortoise''), שילופ (''sloven/slut''), שילוש (''trinity''), שילט / שילטען (''curse''), שילינג / שילינגער (''Polish groschen; English shilling''), and שילער / שילערין (''scholar, pupil'' < MHG schüeler, SL vs SLPL, viable=False), stepping immediately to שימלען (''to mould'') — ZERO *שילאַבער (*shillaber) in 1898 OR 1925 (nybc201108)! Likewise, English-Yiddish p. 563 (leaf n576) steps directly from Shiftless to Shillaloh, Shillaly, Shilling, Shilly-shally, and Shin, and defines Shibboleth (SPLS vs SLPL, viable=False) strictly as biblical Judges 12 test-word (''אַ פּראָבע-װאָרט''), killing the 2012 StackExchange shibboleth guess. Phase-2 cross-check against Harkavy''s 1898 6th edition (completeenglishj00harkuoft) confirmed identical plate text and zero entries for ''*shillaber''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-311.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1898 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
