on Assistant Navy Secretary Theodore Roosevelt''s auxiliary cruiser board (''fit out any shills that might be obtained'' in OCR); high-resolution visual inspection proves the physical newsprint unambiguously reads ''ships''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-218.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1898 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
