PL) matches all four consonant positions (edit distance 0; chronologically plausible: True).", "analysis_notes": "Pushes documented Berlin Rotwelsch Schlepper (''paid steerer who lures victims to gamblers and swindlers'') back 15 years before Ave-Lallemant (1862) to G. W. Zimmermann (1847); cf. p. 429 (Gross 1899). Exact consonant skeleton match SLPL == SLPL.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-101.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-116', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'schlepper', 'contextual_evidence', 'bilingual_contact_context', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-06-07', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_jewish-chronicle_the-jewish-chronicle_1901-06-07_1679/page/n12/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-116.webp', 77532, 'fb5a6e1ced64f2c237a0280b3eca7e4beb62497da3f44f642e0f2be94d726365', '{"id": "CERT-1400-116", "slug": "cert-1400-116", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "schlepper", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "bilingual_contact_context", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "1901-06-07", "sort_date": "1901-06-07", "short_gloss": "Anglo-Jewish press ''schlepper'' retaining initial schl- (Jewish Chronicle 1901)", "source_publication": "The Jewish Chronicle (London), No. 1,679, June 7, 1901, p. 13, col. 1 (IA leaf n12)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_jewish-chronicle_the-jewish-chronicle_1901-06-07_1679/page/n12/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 13, col. 1 (IA leaf n12; front-page masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "The Board of Trade has, at present, no powers to ascertain the religious holdings ... it cannot discriminate between a miserly millionaire and a destitute \"schlepper,\" nor can it state specifically the nationality of any emigrant.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Antedates Green''s Dictionary of Slang for schlepper sense 2 (''pauper / destitute hanger-on'', 1947) by 46 years in English-language Anglo-Jewish journalism, showing late-19th/early-20th-c. Yiddish-English orthographic retention of schl- alongside oral English cluster repair.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-116.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-118', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'ballyhoo', 'contextual_evidence', 'corpus_or_prosopographical_control', 'agent_verified', 1903, '1903-01-01', 'https://digital.library.illinoisstate.edu/digital/collection/p15990coll5/id/11411/', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-118.webp', 180380, '863ebb5c432dfd6b6a9b4c94f9eace8e97a20234d264d0ba91fd790fc8590311', '{"id": "CERT-1200-118", "slug": "cert-1200-118", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "ballyhoo", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "corpus_or_prosopographical_control", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1903, "date_display": "1903", "sort_date": "1903-01-01", "short_gloss": "Archival control: ballyhoo", "source_publication": "The Circus Annual Season 1903: A Route Book of Ringling Brothers'' World''s Greatest Shows (ISU Milner Library Special Collections, Circus Route Books Collection p15990coll5, item 11411), p. 70 (and p. 69 ''booster'')", "source_archive": "Illinois State University Milner Library Digital Collections (p15990coll5)", "source_url": "https://digital.library.illinoisstate.edu/digital/collection/p15990coll5/id/11411/", "page_and_column": "p. 70 (ptr=11406; p. 69 ptr=11405; cover ptr=11335; title ptr=11336)", "verbatim_quote": "LOS ANGELES, Cal., Wednesday and Thursday, September 30th and October 1st.—Great business here. Better than ever. Three turnaways out of four performances. The lot was fully four miles from the business center of the city, but the distance did not serve to keep the masses at home. The parade was the longest of the season, that is, the route was longer, yet it was back on the lot before noon. Considerable trouble was experienced with ticket brokers. They were driven from the lot and \"ballyhoo\" artists were placed at the street car depots to warn the public against them.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1903, "masthead_year": 1903, "linguistic_note": "Negative corpus proof across official circus souvenir route books (1878-1912): 0 tokens of ''shillaber''/''shill'' vs. positive control tokens ''ballyhoo'' (8x) and ''booster'' (9x)", "analysis_notes": "Exhaustive CONTENTdm API full-text sweep (CISOSEARCHALL) across the entire ISU Milner Library Special Collections Circus Route Books archive (p15990coll5: 1878 Sells Bros., 1881-1893 Barnum & Bailey, 1892-1903 Ringling Bros., 1896-1898 Forepaugh-Sells, 1911 Campbell Bros., 1912 Sells-Floto) plus IA Barnum & Bailey / Forepaugh / Robinson route books yields 0 hits for ''shillaber'', ''shillabers'', ''shilaber'', ''shilliber'', ''shilliver'', ''shill'', or ''shills'', whereas positive-control outdoor show terms ''ballyhoo'' (8 hits, e.g. 1903 Ringling p. 70) and ''booster'' (9 hits) appear freely. Explains why ''shillaber'' remained unrecorded in official management souvenir route books (which suppressed ''Sunday-school show''-prohibited grift/decoy terminology) and surfaced first in hostile 1883 Chicago mock-auction exposés before entering open showbiz print in 1908-1910.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-118.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1903 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-305', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'SHILLING', 'hypothesis', 'weakened_or_unlikely_pathway', 'agent_verified', 1903, '1903-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/slangitsanalogue06farmuoft/page/n176/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-305.webp', 120112, '84552e66a79ceee240e5695920a1ad520542ea26e2f6db108278de676cdaf7f5', '{"id": "CERT-1200-305", "slug": "cert-1200-305", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "SHILLING", "record_type": "hypothesis", "record_subtype": "weakened_or_unlikely_pathway", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1903, "date_display": "1903", "sort_date": "1903-01-01", "short_gloss": "Linguistic comparison: SHILLING", "source_publication": "John S. Farmer and W. E. Henley, Slang and Its Analogues Past and Present, Vol. VI (Rea to Stozzle) (London: Printed for Subscribers Only, 1903), p. 175, cols. 1-2 (leaf n176); Joseph Wright, The English Dialect Dictionary, Vol. V (London: Henry Frowde, 1905), p. 384, cols. 1-2 (leaf n395)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/slangitsanalogue06farmuoft/page/n176/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Farmer & Henley Vol. VI (1903), title leaf n2 (''MCMIII''), p. 175 cols. 1-2 (leaf n176); Wright EDD Vol. V (1905), p. 384 cols. 1-2 (leaf n395)", "verbatim_quote": "SHIG, subs. (East End).—In pl. = money: specifically silver. At Winchester SHIG = a shilling (MANSFIELD, c. 1840). SHIGGERS, subs. pl. (Winchester). ... SHIKERRY. See SHICER. SHILLAGALEE, subs. (American).—A loafer. SHILLING. To TAKE THE KING''S (or QUEEN''S) SHILLING, verb. phr. (colloquial).—To enlist. c. 1702. ... SHILLING-SHOCKER (or -DREADFUL) ... SHILLY-SHALLY (also SHALLY-SHALLY), verb. phr. (colloquial).—To trifle...", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": null, "linguistic_note": "Putative derivation of shill / shillaber from (a) British coin shilling (''decoy shilling'' / recruiting sergeant''s ''King''s shilling'' / 1s. mock-auction bid), (b) Hiberno-English shillelagh (''oak cudgel'', conjectured in Jonathan Green''s Crooked Talk [2011]), (c) shilly-shally (''vacillate''), or (d) unattested British dialect *shilliver / *shillober — ALL FALSIFIED.", "analysis_notes": "FALSIFIED-MYTH (1200-C Domain 1 & 2 Comprehensive Compound Audit): Physical ink inspection of Farmer & Henley Vol. VI (leaf n2 ''MCMIII'' = 1903; leaf n176 p. 175) and Wright EDD Vol. V (leaf n395 p. 384) falsifies four recurring folk/published conjectures and confirms zero pre-1908 British dialect *shillaber / *shilliber / *shilliver / *shillober: (1) ''Decoy shilling'' / ''King''s shilling'': No phrase *decoy shilling exists in EDD, Grose, Hotten, Barrère & Leland, or Farmer & Henley; British recruiting ''take the King''s/Queen''s shilling'' denoted military enlistment, never produced *shillaber (SLN vs SLPL < 0.60, viable=False), and U.S. midways/mock auctions operated in dimes/quarters/dollars rather than British shillings. (2) Jonathan Green''s (Crooked Talk, 2011) casual suggestion that shill abbreviates Irish shillelagh (''cudgels the victim into participation'') fails chronologically (ignoring 1883/1908 shillaber, SLK vs SLPL, viable=False) and semantically (shills entice by imitation, never by cudgeling). (3) Tony Thorne''s (2009) archaic ''skill'' conjecture (SKL vs SLPL) and shilly-shally (SLWSLW, vs SL, vs SLPL) likewise fail. (4) EDD Vol. V p. 384 exhaustively lists every genuine British/Irish dialect shill- headword: Shilla/shillar (''gravel/pebbles''), Shillard/shillerd (''a shilling''s worth''), Shill-corn (''blackhead''), Shillelagh, Shillet (''Devonian clay-slate''), Shilling (''ninepence to the shilling'', ''spit shillings''), Shillingther (''shilling''s worth''), Shillock (''coarse knitting''), Shilloo (''Irish outcry''), Shilly (''distort''), Shilly-shally, Shilp, Shilpit — ZERO *shillaber, *shilliber, *shilliver, or *shillober.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-305.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1903 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-107', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Schlepper', 'contextual_evidence', 'bilingual_contact_context', 'agent_verified', 1905, '1905-10-09', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_abendpost-sonntagpost_1905-10-09_17_238/page/n4/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-107.webp', 122134, 'e785cbc300816ea959b96efe7fc3dad22e6b7e255048fd12416f89edfa174424', '{"id": "CERT-1400-107", "slug": "cert-1400-107", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Schlepper", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "bilingual_contact_context", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1905, "date_display": "1905-10-09", "sort_date": "1905-10-09", "short_gloss": "Downtown Chicago bilingual apposition: ''Schlepper („Runner“)'' (Abendpost 1905)", "source_publication": "Abendpost (Chicago, IL), 17. Jahrg., Nr. 238, Oct. 9, 1905, p. 5, col. 4 (IA leaf n4)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_abendpost-sonntagpost_1905-10-09_17_238/page/n4/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 5, col. 4, ''Die Versucher verscheucht.'' (IA leaf n4; front-page masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "Aus dem Viehhofsbezirk sind häufig Klagen darüber eingelaufen, daß die behördlich lizensirten Schlepper („Runner“) von Geschäftshäusern der unteren Stadt, welche dort unter den Viehhändlern und Viehzüchtern nach Kunden suchen, diese oft vom Wege der Tugend verleiten.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": 1905, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Explicit bilingual apposition Schlepper („Runner“) in Chicago German press for six licensed downtown storefront runners (George Morsfield, Frank & Wm. Fish, Frank Reed, Frank Grohe, Moses Löwenstein) steering out-of-town drovers; paired with May 17, 1900 p. 2 (''„Runners“ oder Schlepper'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-107.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1905 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-117', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Shill', 'rejected_lead', 'proper_name_or_homograph', 'agent_verified', 1905, '1905-11-18', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1905-11-18_17_46/page/n10/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-117.webp', 135582, '9202240904389e4eef7f079a3be62c5cd9570c8342bdfc3d311c76ce309aabae', '{"id": "CERT-1200-117", "slug": "cert-1200-117", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Shill", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "proper_name_or_homograph", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1905, "date_display": "1905-11-18", "sort_date": "1905-11-18", "short_gloss": "Rejected lead (proper name or homograph)", "source_publication": "The Billboard (Cincinnati, OH), Vol. 17, No. 46, November 18, 1905, p. 11, col. 3 (Letter List)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1905-11-18_17_46/page/n10/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 11, col. 3 (IA leaf n10; Nov. 18, 1905 cover leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "Shearer, Wm. Sherman, Robt. Sherman, Ralph Sherry, J. W. Shill, Chas. (Show) Short, W. L. Shropshire, James A. Simonson, M. Simpson, E. P. Skidmore, Will", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1905, "masthead_year": 1905, "linguistic_note": "Rejected Trap C showman family surname homograph (''Shill, Chas. (Show)''), owner of ''The Shill Dog, Pony and Vaudeville Show''", "analysis_notes": "Pre-1910 Billboard hits for ''Shill'' + ''Show'' refer to traveling showman Charles Shill, proprietor of ''The Shill Dog, Pony and Vaudeville Show'' (explicitly rostered in The Billboard, Vol. 27, No. 29, July 17, 1915, https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1915-07-17_27_29: ''Chas. Shill, advance and manager; Mary Shill, Chas. Shill, Jr., Ray Shill'')—operating 22 years AFTER ''shillaber'' was already established in 1883 Chicago mock-auction cant (CERT-1200-101). Companion Trap C kills across 1870-1908 newspapers: humorist Benjamin Penhallow Shillaber (''Mrs. Partington''), Capt. Charles E. Shillaber, financier William Shillaber, and Scots agricultural ''shill'' (''shell/peel grain'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-117.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1905 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-219', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shill- ings', 'rejected_lead', 'hyphenation_homograph', 'agent_verified', 1908, '1908-02-08', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_variety_1908-02-08_9_9/page/n9/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-219.webp', 75690, 'eb7196554f43ed632c05b4d1c1c2a0d356ce5210dd5a8e2275f7f4f416422fdb', '{"id": "CERT-1400-219", "slug": "cert-1400-219", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shill- ings", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "hyphenation_homograph", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1908, "date_display": "1908-02-08", "sort_date": "1908-02-08", "short_gloss": "Rejected lead: line-break hyphenated British ''five shill- ings'' (Variety, 8 Feb 1908)", "source_publication": "Variety (New York), Vol. 9, No. 9, Saturday, February 8, 1908, p. 10", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (pub_variety)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_variety_1908-02-08_9_9/page/n9/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 10, col. 1, ''London Notes'' (IA leaf n9; front cover masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "Yesterday afternoon at the Holborn Empire Zbysko threw the Turk, Kara Suliman, twice, winning $500 and packing the hall at prices ranging from five shill- ings to five guineas.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1908, "masthead_year": 1908, "linguistic_note": "FALSIFIED Trap B: End-of-line hyphenation of British currency ''shillings'' (''shill- / ings'')", "analysis_notes": "Explains and kills all pre-1911 ''shill'' full-text hits in pub_variety (1905-1910): every match is a line-wrap hyphenation of British ''shill-ings'' in London music-hall reports. Combined with exhaustive negative sweeps of Show World (all 35 digitized issues, June 1907-Feb. 1908: 0 hits), The Billboard (pre-Mar. 7, 1908: 0 genuine hits), New York Clipper (pre-Mar. 14, 1908: 0 non-surname hits), and National Police Gazette (1878-1907: 0 genuine hits).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-219.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1908 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-120', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shillabers', 'attestation', 'prior_scholarship_witness', 'discovered', 1908, '1908-02-15', 'https://english.stackexchange.com/questions/62859/origin-of-the-word-shill-shillaber', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"id": "CERT-1200-120", "slug": "cert-1200-120", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shillabers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "prior_scholarship_witness", "verification_level": "discovered", "verified_by_agent": null, "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": "Reported by Sven Yargs (2016) & Etymonline; local primary scan not yet archived in DRAgNEt.", "publication_year": 1908, "date_display": "1908-02-15", "sort_date": "1908-02-15", "short_gloss": "Prior-art 1908 carnival cane-rack citation (Sven Yargs / Etymonline)", "source_publication": "Los Angeles Herald (Los Angeles, CA), February 15, 1908 (''Claims Men Are Fakers'', Chronicling America LCCN sn85042462; surfaced by Sven Yargs on English StackExchange Q62859, May 8, 2016)", "source_archive": "Chronicling America (via English StackExchange Q62859 Prior-Art Audit)", "source_url": "https://english.stackexchange.com/questions/62859/origin-of-the-word-shill-shillaber", "page_and_column": "Feb. 15, 1908 (''Fifth and Main streets... cane-and-ring and similar rack gamblers'')", "verbatim_quote": "Frank Perkins, it is alleged, conducted a game in which the players tossed rings at silver money. Simpson and Dwyer are alleged to have been his assistants, known as \"shillabers.\"", "masthead_date_verified": false, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": null, "linguistic_note": "20th-century West Coast street-pitch / cane-and-ring rack-gambling continuation of 1883 Chicago mock-auction ''shillaber''", "analysis_notes": "Logged strictly as BASELINE-LITERATURE per archival verification protocol (LoC endpoint returned HTTP 403 to VM script, so scan_inspected=False): credits researcher Sven Yargs (English StackExchange Q62859, May 8, 2016) for surfacing the Feb. 15, 1908 Los Angeles Herald cane-and-ring ''shillabers'' citation (underlying Etymonline''s ''1908'' baseline in TGT-120, 3 weeks before CERT-1200-103 Billboard Mar. 7, 1908) and Robert Brown''s Apr. 1911 Metropolitan Magazine ''shills'' story (antedated 5 months by CERT-1200-108). Phase-2 NDNP BagIt manifest check (batch_curiv_pescadero_ver01) confirmed that the Library of Congress''s digitized 1908 Los Angeles Herald reel begins on 1 March 1908, explaining the absence of an open NDNP scan for the 15 February 1908 issue.", "scan": {"hosted_path": null, "rights_status": "external_archive_link", "rights_note": "Secondary scholarly baseline; inspect via cited reference URL."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-103', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Shillabers', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1908, '1908-03-07', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1908-03-07_20_10/page/n23/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-103.webp', 113702, 'e97187962f02e1cce75ccc7a41b958350c520ab7bec6054449cbf6d1a741362c', '{"id": "CERT-1200-103", "slug": "cert-1200-103", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Shillabers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1908, "date_display": "1908-03-07", "sort_date": "1908-03-07", "short_gloss": "Outdoor show-trade debut (''No Shillabers'')", "source_publication": "The Billboard (Cincinnati, OH), Vol. 20, No. 10, March 7, 1908, p. 24, col. 4 (display notice for ''The Observations of Doctor Browning'' in Humanity Magazine)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1908-03-07_20_10/page/n23/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 24, col. 4 (IA leaf n23; issue cover leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "WANTED Medicine Men and Medicine Actors And all those who have quituated the medicine show business to read, \"THE OBSERVATIONS OF DOCTOR BROWNING,\" in the current number of \"HUMANITY MAGAZINE.\" It''s the real thing; told in the real thing way. You can buy \"HUMANITY\" on all news stands, for a dime, ten cents. \"Cop the Duckets.\" We are sorry; but no \"Shillabers.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1908, "masthead_year": 1908, "linguistic_note": "Earliest verified outdoor-showman / medicine-show trade-press attestation of ''Shillabers'' (paired with pitchman/circus slang ''quituated'' and ''Cop the Duckets'' = free passes)", "analysis_notes": "Earliest verified show-business trade-paper attestation in The Billboard (March 7, 1908, p. 24; also reprinted in The New York Clipper, Vol. 56, No. 4, March 14, 1908, https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1908-03-14_56_4), following by three weeks Etymonline''s Feb. 15, 1908 Los Angeles Herald mock-auction exposé lead (''Claims Men Are Fakers''). Here ''no \"Shillabers\"'' means no free-pass confederates/deadheads—already foreshadowing the 1910 verb ''shill through'' (''pass in free'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-103.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1908 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-208', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Shillabers', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1908, '1908-03-14', 'https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1908-03-14_56_4/page/n18/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-208.webp', 106476, '4f1b1ef3076a4f2ccd0262c1039f6b8861391919465013edc96b0716624c99a3', '{"id": "CERT-1400-208", "slug": "cert-1400-208", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Shillabers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1908, "date_display": "1908-03-14", "sort_date": "1908-03-14", "short_gloss": "New York theatrical trade-press debut: ''no \"Shillabers\"'' (New York Clipper, 14 Mar 1908)", "source_publication": "The New York Clipper (New York), Vol. 56, No. 4, Saturday, March 14, 1908, p. 119", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (pub_new-york-clipper)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_new-york-clipper_new-york-clipper_1908-03-14_56_4/page/n18/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 119, col. 2, ''WANTED: Medicine Men and Medicine Actors'' (IA leaf n18; masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "You can buy \"HUMANITY\" on all newsstands, for a dime. We give ''em \"the Duckets,\" we are sorry; but no \"Shillabers.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1908, "masthead_year": 1908, "linguistic_note": "Medicine-show / pitchman cant ''Shillabers'' (-5 yrs, 8 mos vs. OED ''shillaber, n.'' Dec. 1913)", "analysis_notes": "Published 7 days after The Billboard (Mar. 7, 1908, CERT-1200-103) and 5 years, 8 months before OED''s Dec. 1913 baseline. Visual inspection also resolves an OCR column-bleed ambiguity: the ad promotes ''The Observations of Doctor Browning'' in the March 1908 issue of Humanity Magazine (St. Louis, MO), distinct from the adjacent col. 3 Tolson Stock Co. notice.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-208.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1908 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-104', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Shillabers', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1909, '1909-04-03', 'https://archive.org/details/filmindex190907film/page/n201/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-104.webp', 138320, '7fcb4c2b6f8756d086192a49e29ec0fc780edc518982c8f9425300a29cfbd5a0', '{"id": "CERT-1200-104", "slug": "cert-1200-104", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Shillabers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1909, "date_display": "1909-04-03", "sort_date": "1909-04-03", "short_gloss": "Nickelodeon & storefront ''shillabers''", "source_publication": "The Film Index (New York: The Films Publishing Co.), Vol. 4, Whole No. 154, April 3, 1909, p. 7, col. 2 (''NOTES.'')", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/filmindex190907film/page/n201/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 7, col. 2 (IA leaf n201; issue masthead leaf n193/n195)", "verbatim_quote": "Nothing short of a \"100 per cent. proposition\" will satiate the appetite for \"soft money\" of the Chicago seceders. * * * \"Shillabers, close up!\" * * * There is a long summer ahead and the penny-wise exhibitor who ties up with the so-called \"independent\" movement will have hard picking ahead.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1909, "masthead_year": 1909, "linguistic_note": "Carnival/sideshow ballyhoo command (''\"Shillabers, close up!\"'') transferred into early nickelodeon / motion-picture trade journalism (-4 yrs, 8 mos vs. OED 1913)", "analysis_notes": "Preserves the literal oral sideshow/barker cue ''\"Shillabers, close up!\"''—instructing decoy patrons to crowd close to the ballyhoo platform/ticket-box—deployed metaphorically against Chicago independent film exchanges without glossing, proving showbiz readers in April 1909 already knew the carnival routine.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-104.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1909 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-214', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'booster', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1909, '1909-09-25', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1909-09-25_21_39/page/n2/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-214.webp', 166334, '4bdb06800fbc8c836323de2df970f25f9df92c81eb907745309e8fc9627d8af4', '{"id": "CERT-1200-214", "slug": "cert-1200-214", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "booster", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1909, "date_display": "1909-09-25", "sort_date": "1909-09-25", "short_gloss": "Carnival transition from ''shillaber'' to ''booster''", "source_publication": "The Billboard (Cincinnati, OH), Vol. 21, No. 39, September 25, 1909, p. 4", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_billboard_1909-09-25_21_39/page/n2/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 4, col. 3 (IA leaf n2; paired on plate with Mar. 7, 1908 p. 24)", "verbatim_quote": "One booster would crowd into the board and win out a five or a ten. He would come out and stand idly, with the money in his hand, and his hands behind him. The boss booster would touch him on the hand, he would let go of the money, and the boss booster would take it around and hand it to the inside man, and soon the booster would again win the same piece of money.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": null, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Documents ''booster'' and ''boss booster'' operating the exact secret prize-recycling loop on a 1909 county-fair pickout booth that ''shillabers or \"shills\"'' executed in 1911 (CERT-1200-111). Deduplicated against CERT-1200-103 (Mar. 7, 1908 Billboard p. 24). Proof plate bottom panel: CERT-1200-214_billboard_1908_03_07_shillabers_1909_booster.png.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-214.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1909 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-105', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shillaber', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_green-book-magazine_1910-01_3_1/page/n66/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-105.webp', 172482, 'c5fbea9babe497e488d2ee3ae6d4b0adca58e7eb341feabc87b06b541cb67327', '{"id": "CERT-1200-105", "slug": "cert-1200-105", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shillaber", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-01", "sort_date": "1910-01-01", "short_gloss": "Circus midway outside decoy (''shillaber'')", "source_publication": "Walter Prichard Eaton, ''The Psychology of the Ballyhoo'', The Green Book Album (Chicago: The Story-Press Corp.), Vol. 3, No. 1, January 1910, p. 66, col. 1", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_green-book-magazine_1910-01_3_1/page/n66/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 66, col. 1 (IA leaf n66; January 1910 contents masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "Many women tourists, seeing them there, say to themselves, \"Well, if those women can ride without an escort it''s all right for me to\" and pay their dollar. When the wagon is filled, watch, and you will see the first lone females climb out and wait for the next empty car. Down at Coney Island \"live bait\" is known by a different name—the old circus name, \"shillaber.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Explicit metalinguistic testimony identifying ''shillaber'' in January 1910 as ''the old circus name'' transferred to Coney Island midways and functionally analogous to sight-seeing (''rubberneck'') wagon decoy passengers (''live bait'')", "analysis_notes": "Crucial socio-historical bridge: drama critic Walter Prichard Eaton contrasts sight-seeing ''rubberneck wagon'' decoy riders (''live bait'') with Coney Island midway decoys bearing ''the old circus name, \"shillaber.\"'' Simultaneously antedates OED (1913) by nearly four years and proves that while vehicle-decoy mechanics existed on excursion wagons, contemporaries viewed ''shillaber'' specifically as old circus sideshow argot rather than sight-seeing-bus jargon.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-105.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-205', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shillaber', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_green-book-magazine_1910-01_3_1/page/n66/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-205.webp', 214150, '11c657c92e9bee1775defe7c2f1c44246e993b63bdd9a99640b1df70b9955f0f', '{"id": "CERT-1200-205", "slug": "cert-1200-205", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shillaber", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910", "sort_date": "1910-01-01", "short_gloss": "Sightseeing ''rubberneck wagon'' decoy (''shillaber'')", "source_publication": "Walter Prichard Eaton, ''The Psychology of the Ballyhoo'', The Green Book Album: A Magazine of the Passing Show (Chicago: Story-Press Corp.), Vol. 3, No. 1, January 1910, pp. 63-67", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_green-book-magazine_1910-01_3_1/page/n66/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 66, col. 2 (IA leaf n66; Jan. 1910 contents masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "They mingle with the crowds, drift up to the ticket seller, pretend to buy tickets (it is said they used to say to him, as a password, \"shillaber,\" hence the name) and then file in at the entrance. Then they come out again by the back way and repeat the process.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": null, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Distinct col. 2 companion to CERT-1200-105 (col. 1): records the earliest printed showman folk-etymology claiming sideshow decoys whispered ''shillaber'' as a gate password before silent fingertip signals (CERT-1200-110) took over. Printed pagination corrected to p. 66 via Jan. 1910 Table of Contents (''The Psychology of the Ballyhoo... 63''). Proof plate: CERT-1200-205_green_book_1910_01_rubberneck_wagon_shillaber.png.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-205.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-106', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shill through', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-05-14', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n13/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-106.webp', 81948, 'cacac4f2baa0fe395cc7b23540cfbe5b2ce45a5c5356255414ef594ff013a5c8', '{"id": "CERT-1200-106", "slug": "cert-1200-106", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shill through", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-05-14", "sort_date": "1910-05-14", "short_gloss": "Earliest verb phrase (''shill through'')", "source_publication": "George Randolph Chester, ''Ballyhoo Bill'', The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia: Curtis Publishing Co.), Vol. 182, No. 46, May 14, 1910, pp. 12-14, 65", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n13/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 12, col. 3 (IA leaf n13; May 14, 1910 cover leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "\"Just ordinary business affairs,\" replied the veteran fair manager, smiling. \"That tall young fellow is a side-show barker, or outside lecturer, as they call themselves, and he looks to be a good one. He is out of a job and tried to shill through your gate. A shillaber is a booster for a sideshow, and, consequently, to go in free anywhere is to shill through.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Back-formed / clipped verb ''shill'' (''shill through'') explicitly derived in-text from sideshow noun ''shillaber'' (''A shillaber is a booster for a sideshow, and, consequently, to go in free anywhere is to shill through'')", "analysis_notes": "Documents the exact morphological clipping moment in print: the clipped stem ''shill'' emerges first as a verbal clipping (''to shill through'') from ''shillaber'' on county-fair / circus-sideshow midways six months before our earliest clipped noun ''shill'' (Nov. 19, 1910).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-106.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-119', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shilled', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-05-14', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n15/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-119.webp', 96482, '5bdb89aacd5ee54cc41890da13ddfb31849cae5711eff343a4408f0b6e0e69d3', '{"id": "CERT-1200-119", "slug": "cert-1200-119", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shilled", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-05-14", "sort_date": "1910-05-14", "short_gloss": "Earliest past-tense verb (''shilled in'')", "source_publication": "George Randolph Chester, ''Ballyhoo Bill'', The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia: Curtis Publishing Co.), Vol. 182, No. 46, May 14, 1910, pp. 12-14, 65", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n15/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 14, col. 1 (IA leaf n15; May 14, 1910 cover leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "\"It''s a rummy outfit for fair,\" agreed Hoover; \"but I can pull in the kale with it—if the money''s here.\" \"There''s grubbin''s,\" said the Colonel, \"but I queered myself on the jump. The mayor shilled in the first openin'' and I talked with him and he seemed to be easy; so I give him the works.\" \"Blow-off too?\" \"Blow-off too.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": null, "linguistic_note": "Verbal conversion and preterite inflection (''shilled in'') from carnival sideshow ''shillaber'' -> ''shill through / shill in''", "analysis_notes": "Earliest verified preterite/finite verb ''shilled'' (''The mayor shilled in the first openin''''), antedating OED shill, v.3 (1914) by 4 years and Green''s earliest inflected ''shilled'' (1916, Jack Lait ''having shilled'') by 6 years. Masthead (leaf n0) and printed running footer (''14 THE SATURDAY EVENING POST May 14, 1910'', leaf n15) verified on physical ink.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-119.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-215', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shillaber brigade', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-05-14', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n15/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-215.webp', 129680, 'ed4c7ddff9e1feaf1d0fda802b83aabfe4e54779fbe36ddeda775ea26fda5648', '{"id": "CERT-1200-215", "slug": "cert-1200-215", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shillaber brigade", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-05-14", "sort_date": "1910-05-14", "short_gloss": "Collocation ''shillaber brigade'' + verbal ''shill through''", "source_publication": "George Randolph Chester, ''Ballyhoo Bill'', The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia: Curtis Publishing Co.), Vol. 182, No. 46, May 14, 1910, pp. 12-14, 65", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-05-14_182_46/page/n15/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 14, col. 2 (IA leaf n15; cover leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "PROFESSOR SKYBO began his fusillade of blank revolver shots as soon as Mr. Hoover hove in sight, and with the first shot the shillaber brigade came running from all corners, their haste and apparent excitement inducing newcomers to follow them.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": null, "masthead_year": null, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Earliest attested attributive compound ''shillaber brigade'' (3 years, 7 months before OED shillaber, n. 1913) depicting the coordinated sideshow rush triggered by blank revolver shots. Story title verified on printed p. 12 as ''Ballyhoo Bill'' (correcting ''Spoiling the Egyptians''). Proof plate bottom panel: CERT-1200-215_sat_eve_post_1910_05_14_shillaber_shill_through.png.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-215.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-107', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Shillers', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-07-09', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-07-09_183_2/page/n6/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-107.webp', 90620, '1ed0e1f41acbf78491283ed2ebf83395a868367b1e775fc386127832301f910a', '{"id": "CERT-1200-107", "slug": "cert-1200-107", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Shillers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-07-09", "sort_date": "1910-07-09", "short_gloss": "Agentive derivative (''Shillers'')", "source_publication": "Isaac F. Marcosson, ''In the Good Old Summertime: Profits in Making People Laugh'', The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia: Curtis Publishing Co.), Vol. 183, No. 2, July 9, 1910, pp. 3-5", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1910-07-09_183_2/page/n6/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 5, col. 1 (IA leaf n6; July 9, 1910 cover leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "what are known in the summer amusement vernacular as \"shillabers.\" In the gambling fraternity they would be \"come-ons.\" When the \"barker\" has finished his opening talk, or \"made an opening\" as it is called, and has failed to \"turn them\"—that is, get people inside—you will hear him yell, \"Shillers to the fore.\" In a moment several men and women will walk briskly up to the ticket seller, buy tickets and step into the show with great assurance and confidence. They are the \"shillabers\" employed by the park.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Transitional ''-er'' agentive shortening ''Shillers'' co-occurring in the same paragraph with ''shillabers'', gambling ''come-ons'', ''barker'', and ''ballyhoo''", "analysis_notes": "Captures the intermediate agentive reduction ''shillabers'' -> ''Shillers'' in the barker''s shouted rally cry ''\"Shillers to the fore\"'' during the summer amusement-park ballyhoo ticket rush.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-107.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-209', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'Shillabers', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-09-12', 'https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ndnp/ndhi/batch_ndhi_deering_ver01/data/sn85042373/00212475865/1910091201/0604.xml', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-209.webp', 120560, '171a77ea025b1a4d0cadd271caba7b995acdfa680d71444ee03ea9cc098042d8', '{"id": "CERT-1400-209", "slug": "cert-1400-209", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "Shillabers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-09-12", "sort_date": "1910-09-12", "short_gloss": "Prize-ring extension: ''for the benefit of the Shillabers'' (12 Sep 1910)", "source_publication": "The Evening Times (Grand Forks, ND), Vol. 5, No. 215, Monday, September 12, 1910, p. 3", "source_archive": "Library of Congress Chronicling America / NDNP Static Storage (batch_ndhi_deering_ver01)", "source_url": "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ndnp/ndhi/batch_ndhi_deering_ver01/data/sn85042373/00212475865/1910091201/0604.xml", "page_and_column": "p. 3, col. 1, ''Blacks May Get Together Next'' (NDNP frame 0604; masthead p. 1 frame 0602)", "verbatim_quote": "Here is one section of the Woodman bulletin: \"The next big fight for the benefit of the Shillabers will be between Jack Johnson and Sam Langford. Don''t overlook this.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Sporting/prize-ring transfer of ''Shillabers'' (-3 yrs, 2 mos vs. OED ''shillaber, n.'' Dec. 1913)", "analysis_notes": "Retrieved directly via NDNP static storage (batch_ndhi_deering_ver01, LCCN sn85042373). Quotes Boston boxing manager Joe Woodman (manager of Sam Langford) extending ''Shillabers'' into syndicated prize-ring publicity 3 years, 2 months prior to OED''s first citation.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-209.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-201', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'fake auction', 'contextual_evidence', 'syndicate_provenance', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-09-23', 'https://archive.org/details/per_chicago-daily-tribune_1910-09-23_69_228/page/n8/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-201.webp', 95408, '71e5d960002108f56649fab7bf2ba6400a8e6d2667e4011199bf2093707a755b', '{"id": "CERT-1400-201", "slug": "cert-1400-201", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "fake auction", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "syndicate_provenance", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-09-23", "sort_date": "1910-09-23", "short_gloss": "Newsstand release proof: Oct. 1910 Pearson''s Magazine ''The Fake Auction'' by H. E. Twinells", "source_publication": "The Chicago Daily Tribune, Vol. 69, No. 228, Friday, September 23, 1910, p. 9", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (pub_chicago-daily-tribune)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_chicago-daily-tribune_1910-09-23_69_228/page/n8/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 9, display advertisement (IA leaf n8; masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "PEARSON''S MAGAZINE now on sale. ... the difference between a fake auction and a genuine auction is explained by H. E. Twinells.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Syndicate provenance proof pinning H. E. Twinells''s ''The Fake Auction'' (Pearson''s Magazine, Vol. 24, No. 4, Oct. 1910) to newsstand sale on or before September 23, 1910", "analysis_notes": "Contemporaneous display notice in The Chicago Daily Tribune (Sept. 23, 1910, leaf n8; corroborated by The New York Times Saturday Review of Books, Sept. 24, 1910, https://archive.org/details/newyorktimesbook0000vari/page/n589/mode/1up) proves that H. E. Twinells''s ''The Fake Auction''—the source text behind the Feb. 1911 syndicated boilerplate feature in CERT-1200-109—was published in the October 1910 issue of Pearson''s Magazine (New York) on or before Sept. 23, 1910 (-4.8 months earlier than CERT-1200-109).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-201.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-210', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shillabers', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-10-13', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_leslies-weekly_1910-10-13_111_2875/page/n9/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-210.webp', 75648, '35acfbb41ee294fd3609078c12da0f6acad3197bb085a987e06ff3f309f5c5df', '{"id": "CERT-1400-210", "slug": "cert-1400-210", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shillabers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-10-13", "sort_date": "1910-10-13", "short_gloss": "Unquoted underworld taxonomy: ''Criminals, shillabers, cadets'' (Leslie''s Weekly, 13 Oct 1910)", "source_publication": "Leslie''s Illustrated Weekly (New York), Vol. 111, No. 2875, October 13, 1910, p. 374", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_microfilm)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_leslies-weekly_1910-10-13_111_2875/page/n9/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 374, col. 3, ''Does the Pistol Make the Criminal?'' by John Wilmer Broadman (IA leaf n9; cover leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "Criminals, shillabers, cadets, bar flies, panhandlers, lawless foreigners and other types of vagabonds, would give the most thought to the subject and provide themselves with the best weapons.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "NYC municipal/Pinkerton underworld taxonomy ''shillabers'' (-3 yrs, 1 mo vs. OED Dec. 1913)", "analysis_notes": "Essay drawing on Pinkerton National Detective Agency New York homicide files lists ''shillabers'' without quotation marks or gloss alongside ''cadets'', ''bar flies'', and ''panhandlers'', demonstrating naturalized New York underworld currency by autumn 1910 (-3 yrs, 1 mo vs. OED).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-210.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1200-108', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shill', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-11-19', 'https://archive.org/details/fort-wayne-sentinel-1910-11-19/page/n23/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-108.webp', 175000, '5151e7b1ba87053a64a23cf447a104a8afc8c95dd86d7d6f9a8e1afea4c61c78', '{"id": "CERT-1200-108", "slug": "cert-1200-108", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shill", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1200-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-11-19", "sort_date": "1910-11-19", "short_gloss": "Earliest clipped simplex noun (''a shill'')", "source_publication": "The Fort Wayne Sentinel (Fort Wayne, IN), Saturday Evening, November 19, 1910, p. 24, col. 3 (''BOOSTING the GAME'')", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/fort-wayne-sentinel-1910-11-19/page/n23/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 24, col. 3 (IA leaf n23; Nov. 19, 1910 front masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "The auction room is a breeding place for the \"plugger,\" though in its case his technical name is a \"shill,\" and his duty is to lure on to high bids the occasional \"sucker\" who ventures within.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Clipped monosyllabic noun ''shill'' (< ''shillaber''), explicitly identified in November 1910 as the mock-auction room''s ''technical name'' for a decoy bidder", "analysis_notes": "Pushes the clipped simplex noun ''shill'' back into 1910, predating both OED''s 1916 baseline (by over five years) and Etymonline''s ''by 1911, in newspaper exposés of fake auctions'' benchmark.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1200-108.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-206', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shills', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-11-19', 'https://archive.org/details/fort-wayne-sentinel-1910-11-19/page/n23/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-206.webp', 101012, '1893a9e154b84496444b91d27c52dfe9bf67a8949fd1e588bbd0624cd6ae6d91', '{"id": "CERT-1400-206", "slug": "cert-1400-206", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shills", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-11-19", "sort_date": "1910-11-19", "short_gloss": "New York Herald Syndicate credit (''By Garnet Warren'') & plural ''shills'' (19 Nov 1910)", "source_publication": "The Fort Wayne Sentinel (Fort Wayne, IN), Saturday, November 19, 1910, p. 24", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/fort-wayne-sentinel-1910-11-19/page/n23/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 24, cols. 1 & 5 (IA leaf n23; masthead p. 1 leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "BY GARNET WARREN. (Copyright, 1910, by the New York Herald Co. All rights reserved.) ... The \"shills\" work each auction room for a day or so and then move about elsewhere, for their services are in great demand.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Plural ''shills'' (-5 yrs, 2 mos vs. OED ''shill, n.'' 1916) in New York Herald Syndicate feature", "analysis_notes": "Full-page visual inspection of p. 24 recovers the printed byline and copyright stamp missed in Wave 5 OCR: ''BY GARNET WARREN. / (Copyright, 1910, by the New York Herald Co. All rights reserved.)'', proving that ''BOOSTING the GAME'' originated in James Gordon Bennett''s New York Herald (Herald Square, NYC) and was distributed by the New York Herald Syndicate, while also plating plural ''shills'' (''standing thickly clustered about the verdant young person... The \"shills\" work each auction room'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-206.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1400-211', 'TGT-120', 'shill-shillaber', NULL, 'shill / shillaber', 'shillabers', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-11-20', 'https://archive.org/details/per_chicago-daily-tribune_1910-11-20_69_47/page/n26/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-211.webp', 100034, 'a35ca7866a444c2be9abe26d2005916779d42da7ad2511bbf83d557ba99ecdeb', '{"id": "CERT-1400-211", "slug": "cert-1400-211", "case_slug": "shill-shillaber", "headword": "shill / shillaber", "attested_form": "shillabers", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1400-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "1910-11-20", "sort_date": "1910-11-20", "short_gloss": "Chicago sports verse pairing ''cappers'', ''boosters'', and ''shillabers'' (20 Nov 1910)", "source_publication": "The Chicago Sunday Tribune (Chicago), Vol. 69, No. 47, Sunday, November 20, 1910, Sporting Section", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (pub_chicago-daily-tribune)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_chicago-daily-tribune_1910-11-20_69_47/page/n26/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Sporting Section, col. 4 (IA leaf n26; front-page masthead leaf n0)", "verbatim_quote": "We''d get right at the cappers and the boosters of the game, / The shillabers and shysters from no matter where they came, / And no matter how they framed it it would look to us the same.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Chicago sporting verse pairing ''cappers'', ''boosters'', and ''shillabers'' (-3 yrs vs. OED Dec. 1913)", "analysis_notes": "Exhaustive audit of all 94 pre-1914 ''shillaber(s)'' hits in pub_chicago-daily-tribune confirms this Nov. 20, 1910 verse is the first non-surname return of ''shillabers'' to The Chicago Tribune after June 7, 1883 (CERT-1200-102), explicitly co-indexing ''cappers'', ''boosters'', and ''shillabers''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/shill-shillaber/CERT-1400-211.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (on or before Dec. 31, 1930); in the United States public domain as of Jan. 1, 2026."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
