ments in 1861 for a quartermaster''s or soldier''s shanty/outfit", "analysis_notes": "Urban sporting-press substrate proof #4 (New York, May 5, 1860; cf. also April 17, 1858 Clipper ''shebeens''): Proves the exact New York sporting weekly that popularized ''chebang'' (Aug. 1859) and ''Shebang'' (Sept. & Dec. 1860; June & Dec. 1861) simultaneously used ''\"shebeen\"'' for a low unlicensed whiskey cabin.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/whole-shebang/CERT-2000-117.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1860 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
