r soldier''s shanty/outfit", "analysis_notes": "Primary-scan-verified (-2y vs. 1862 baseline; caught via dirty-OCR regex where IA OCR misread ''Shebang'' as ''Bhebang''). Establishes ''Shebang'' as the standard New York-Baltimore concert-saloon term for Charles Percival''s Pagoda music hall (lager, cigars, minstrel & ballet acts).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/whole-shebang/CERT-2000-108.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1860 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-2000-224', 'TGT-044', 'whole-shebang', NULL, 'whole shebang', 'Shebang', 'rejected_lead', 'ocr_ghost', 'agent_verified', 1860, '1860-11-27', 'https://panewsarchive.psu.edu/lccn/sn83032304/1860-11-27/ed-1/seq-3/', 1, '/scans/whole-shebang/CERT-2000-224.webp', 195764, '6b43fa8c9407db1e04913cf378055fd0325ae4a97db4f8c1f673f7f1fdcd61b2', '{"id": "CERT-2000-224", "slug": "cert-2000-224", "case_slug": "whole-shebang", "headword": "whole shebang", "attested_form": "Shebang", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "ocr_ghost", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt Archival Pipeline", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1860, "date_display": "27 Nov 1860", "sort_date": "1860-11-27", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: Shebang", "source_publication": "The Lancaster Intelligencer (Lancaster City, PA), Vol. LXI, No. 46, Tuesday Morning, November 27, 1860", "source_archive": "Pennsylvania Newspaper Archive / Penn State Open-ONI (LCCN sn83032304)", "source_url": "https://panewsarchive.psu.edu/lccn/sn83032304/1860-11-27/ed-1/seq-3/", "page_and_column": "p. 3, col. 5 (''Valuable City Property For Sale — No. 2 East Orange Street'')", "verbatim_quote": "[Corrupted Open-ONI OCR layer:] ''containing Hall, Parlor, Dining lisAii, 2 Shebang\" with Range, and 2 Pantries on 1st floor'' — [Actual printed ink on Nov. 27, 1860 scan:] ''containing Hall, Parlor, Dining Room, 2 Kitchens with Range, and 2 Pantries on 1st floor; 5 Chambers with Bath &c., on 2d floor''.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1860, "masthead_year": 1860, "linguistic_note": "Anglo-Irish shebeen (''unlicensed tavern/shanty'', < Irish síbín) -> antebellum U.S. urban saloon/shanty slang chebang/shebang (1852-1861) -> Civil War Union camp hut/establishment -> collective phrasal idiom ''the whole chebang / shebang'' (1863-1867)", "analysis_notes": "CRITICAL TRAP B & TRAP A FALSIFICATION CONTROL! Because Lancaster County is the exact home county of the 1861 Columbia Spy camp letters (CERT-2000-201, 203, 204), an unverified OCR hit in the Nov. 27, 1860 Lancaster Intelligencer (''Dining lisAii, 2 Shebang\" with Range'') looked dangerously like a pre-war Lancaster domestic-architecture precursor. Direct inspection of the high-resolution page scan proves the physical ink unambiguously reads ''Dining Room, 2 Kitchens with Range, and 2 Pantries on 1st floor'' (worn type on ''Kitchens'' hallucinated by OCR into ''Shebang\"''). Companion Trap B & Trap A kills documented during the 1860-1872 sweep: (1) Pittsburgh Daily Post, Aug. 21, 1861, p. 1 OCR ''Shebang'' -> physical ink reads ''Shafting'' (machinery); (2) Pittsburgh Gazette, Oct. 30, 1866, p. 4 OCR ''Shebang Lodge, I.O.O.F.'' -> physical ink reads ''Shenango Lodge, I.O.O.F.''; (3) Google Books americanmedical15unkngoog metadata ''1860'' -> true masthead July 4, 1863 (Vol. VII, No. 1); (4) IA sim_los-angeles-times_1862-03-07_81 metadata ''1862'' -> true masthead March 7, 1962 (Vol. LXXXI); (5) IA farmingbusiness4445unse metadata ''1872'' -> true masthead April 29, 1916.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/whole-shebang/CERT-2000-224.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1860 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
