12, 1900.'' Attests ''yeggmen'' (3x) and ''yeggman'' (2x) on arrest of John Butler alias ''Frisco Slim'', with zero mention of ''John Yegg'' or St. Paul.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-201.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1900 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-109', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1900, '1900-09-08', 'https://archive.org/details/cssf_000277/page/n1/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-109.webp', 204232, '06694bed528d8b052cab41a3b8e5e36cb3a18e016feb529c0817862e38029b71', '{"id": "CERT-1500-109", "slug": "cert-1500-109", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1900, "date_display": "8 Sep 1900", "sort_date": "1900-09-08", "short_gloss": "yegg in The Enterprise (South San Francisco, CA)", "source_publication": "The Enterprise (South San Francisco, CA)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (California Revealed)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/cssf_000277/page/n1/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 5, No. 45, p. 2, cols. 5-6 (leaf 1)", "verbatim_quote": "These ''hobo'' criminals are called ''yeggs'' or ''Johnny Yeggmen.'' ... The ''gay cat'' occupies a position midway between that of the ''cat'' and the ''yegg.''", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1900, "masthead_year": 1900, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, n. (1903, -3y). Syndicated illustrated feature (''HOBO CRIME EXPERTS'', also translated into German in Chicago Abendpost, 25 Sept. 1900, p. 5, https://archive.org/details/sim_abendpost-sonntagpost_1900-09-25_12_228) quoting W. A. Pinkerton on ''Topeka Joe''; earliest verified print attestation of ''Johnny Yeggmen'' and non-attributive singular count noun ''the yegg'', published nearly a month before the Oct. 2-4, 1900 ABA convention.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-109.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1900 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-202', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Johnny Yeggmen', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1900, '1900-09-08', 'https://archive.org/details/cssf_000277/page/n1/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-202.webp', 130116, 'e4c149077ed77a477da3e42b98d16868d7e44e5eb8a070103aae5f1806f882ca', '{"id": "CERT-1500-202", "slug": "cert-1500-202", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Johnny Yeggmen", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1900, "date_display": "8 Sep 1900", "sort_date": "1900-09-08", "short_gloss": "Johnny Yeggmen in The Enterprise (South San Francisco, CA), ''HOBO CRIME EXPERTS ... Are Known to Detectives Under the Name of Yeggmen''", "source_publication": "The Enterprise (South San Francisco, CA), ''HOBO CRIME EXPERTS ... Are Known to Detectives Under the Name of Yeggmen''", "source_archive": "Internet Archive California Digital Newspaper Collection (cssf_000277, leaves 0-1)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/cssf_000277/page/n1/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 5, No. 45, p. 2, cols. 5-6", "verbatim_quote": "nearly every one of these crimes was committed by tramp operatives known in prison and police parlance as ''yeggs'' or ''Johnny Yeggmen.''", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1900, "masthead_year": 1900, "linguistic_note": "Generic underworld ''Johnny X'' placeholder compound (''Johnny Yeggmen'' / ''yeggs'') in prison and police parlance", "analysis_notes": "Masthead verified: Saturday, Sept. 8, 1900. Syndicated Chicago interview with W. A. Pinkerton following arrest of ''Topeka Joe''. Lists 32 road aliases without naming any ''John Yegg'', proving ''yeggs'' and ''Johnny Yeggmen'' were already established generic plural terms before the Oct. 1900 ABA convention.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-202.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1900 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-203', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yeggmen', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1900, '1900-09-25', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_abendpost-sonntagpost_1900-09-25_12_228/page/n5/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-203.webp', 237818, '64242513ec306d78d2e95bedc0e62719f36f1fc5f82b5cb91ca7cdfff3c4b8ab', '{"id": "CERT-1500-203", "slug": "cert-1500-203", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yeggmen", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1900, "date_display": "25 Sep 1900", "sort_date": "1900-09-25", "short_gloss": "Yeggmen in Abendpost (Chicago, IL), ''Bei den Yeggmen / Verbrecherische Tramps''", "source_publication": "Abendpost (Chicago, IL), ''Bei den Yeggmen / Verbrecherische Tramps''", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_abendpost-sonntagpost_1900-09-25_12_228, leaf 5)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_abendpost-sonntagpost_1900-09-25_12_228/page/n5/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Jg. 12, No. 228, p. 6, col. 5", "verbatim_quote": "Aus ganz anderem Holz sind die aggressiven Stromer geschnitzt, die \"Yeggmen\", wahrscheinlich ein Verzweiflungsprodukt des Stromerlebens!", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1900, "masthead_year": 1900, "linguistic_note": "English plural ''Yeggmen'' & singular ''Yeggman'' borrowed as American police slang into Chicago German newsprint", "analysis_notes": "Notice a Chicago German-language daily treats ''Yeggmen'' as unfamiliar English detective terminology rather than recognizing it as German Jager.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-203.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1900 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-204', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'sneak thieves', 'contextual_evidence', 'corpus_or_prosopographical_control', 'agent_verified', 1900, '1900-10-13', 'https://fraser.stlouisfed.org/files/docs/publications/cfc/cfc_19001013_supplement.pdf', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-204.webp', 163960, '4816d51c4b52827aa7893d4ac0a455f5a0a36a806b811e01191ae3398e5f6e75', '{"id": "CERT-1500-204", "slug": "cert-1500-204", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "sneak thieves", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "corpus_or_prosopographical_control", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1900, "date_display": "13 Oct 1900", "sort_date": "1900-10-13", "short_gloss": "Contextual Evidence: sneak thieves (The Bankers'' Magazine, Vol. 61, No. 4 (Oct. 1900) & Commercial and Financial Chronicle: Bankers'' and Tru", "source_publication": "The Bankers'' Magazine, Vol. 61, No. 4 (Oct. 1900) & Commercial and Financial Chronicle: Bankers'' and Trust Supplement, Vol. 71, No. 1842 (Oct. 13, 1900), p. 62", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_bankers-magazine_1900-10_61_4, leaf 64) & FRASER Federal Reserve Archive", "source_url": "https://fraser.stlouisfed.org/files/docs/publications/cfc/cfc_19001013_supplement.pdf", "page_and_column": "CFC Supplement p. 62; Bankers'' Magazine p. 545", "verbatim_quote": "At noonday on August 9, 1899, the Scandinavian-American Bank, of St. Paul, Minn., a member of the association, was robbed of $540 in currency by sneak thieves, one of whom called the temporary occupant of the teller''s cage to the telephone, while the other stepped from the lobby to the window and fished the money through. The thieves returned the money with an anonymous note saying that the theft would never have occurred had the membership sign been displayed at the teller''s window.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1900, "masthead_year": 1900, "linguistic_note": "Falsifies safe-blowing premise of St. Paul ''John Yegg'' origin story", "analysis_notes": "Proves from the 1900 ABA Protective Committee''s own report (Richmond convention, Oct. 2-4, 1900; also bound in HathiTrust mdp.39015077845397) that the Aug. 9, 1899 St. Paul robbery was a daytime telephone-distraction sneak-theft through the teller''s window, not a yegg nitroglycerin safe-burglary.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-204.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1900 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-110', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yeggs', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-01-24', 'https://archive.org/details/xt7qbz616q6h/page/n1/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-110.webp', 171104, '558be30375ad97e3660f6e766f03d2cd80f98950a7476139046a10448f7f5cc5', '{"id": "CERT-1500-110", "slug": "cert-1500-110", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yeggs", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "24 Jan 1901", "sort_date": "1901-01-24", "short_gloss": "yeggs in The Bee (Earlington, KY)", "source_publication": "The Bee (Earlington, KY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (University of Kentucky)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/xt7qbz616q6h/page/n1/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 2, col. 2 (leaf 1; masthead p. 4, leaf 3)", "verbatim_quote": "It will be remembered that the Marshal of Ludlow and a Deputy arrested in that village four men who were thought to be \"yeggs.\" The big fellow, who seemed to be the leader of the gang", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, n. (1903, -2y; also predates Josiah Flynt''s Feb. 1901 McClure''s Magazine article and Sept. 1901 NYT). Covington, KY dispatch dated Jan. 21, 1901 using simplex plural ''yeggs'' in regional Kentucky rail-junction press.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-110.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
