of Graft: Chicago'' (reprinted in book form in The World of Graft, 1901, p. 27, https://archive.org/details/cu31924030315943). Attested spelling set to ''Yegg'' (stem of hyphenated ''Yegg-men'') per harness hyphen-normalization rule.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-111.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-207', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yegg', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-02-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_new-mcclures-magazine_1901-02_16_4/page/n46/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-207.webp', 139376, '45b3bc8eb1307833552031a6b943a27504fbbe08d902a48f993eab92394db30b', '{"id": "CERT-1500-207", "slug": "cert-1500-207", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "Feb 1901", "sort_date": "1901-02-01", "short_gloss": "Yegg in Josiah Flynt, ''In the World of Graft: I. Chi, An Honest City'', McClure''s Magazine, Vol. 16, No. 4 (Feb. 1901)", "source_publication": "Josiah Flynt, ''In the World of Graft: I. Chi, An Honest City'', McClure''s Magazine, Vol. 16, No. 4 (Feb. 1901)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_new-mcclures-magazine_1901-02_16_4, leaf 46)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_new-mcclures-magazine_1901-02_16_4/page/n46/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 333, cols. 1-2 (''THE UNDEFINED YEGG-MEN'')", "verbatim_quote": "The great majority are what certain detectives call \"Yegg-men,\" which is a term, by the way, that the detectives would do well to define. As far as I can discover it means tramp-thieves, but the average tramp seldom uses the word.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Detective-popularized cant designation (''what certain detectives call Yegg-men'')", "analysis_notes": "Crucial sociolinguistic testimony from America''s foremost tramp ethnographer: in Feb. 1901 Flynt notes detectives popularized ''Yegg-men'' whereas ''the average tramp seldom uses the word''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-207.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-112', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yeggmen', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-05-16', 'https://gahistoricnewspapers.galileo.usg.edu/lccn/sn89053684/1901-05-16/ed-1/seq-4/', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-112.webp', 93192, '56d108045a57def879305667ce8197ff5e63ad9326159ddef907f7800a3f3244', '{"id": "CERT-1500-112", "slug": "cert-1500-112", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yeggmen", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "16 May 1901", "sort_date": "1901-05-16", "short_gloss": "yeggmen in The Savannah Morning News (Savannah, GA)", "source_publication": "The Savannah Morning News (Savannah, GA)", "source_archive": "Georgia Historic Newspapers (Open-ONI / UGA IIIF)", "source_url": "https://gahistoricnewspapers.galileo.usg.edu/lccn/sn89053684/1901-05-16/ed-1/seq-4/", "page_and_column": "p. 4, col. 3", "verbatim_quote": "The especial enemies of the country banks are what Robert Pinkerton calls \"yeggmen.\" The name comes from John Yegg, a California tramp who turned bank burglar.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, n. (1903, -2y). Summarizing May 1901 Northwestern Banker article; earliest verified newspaper printing of Robert Pinkerton''s ''John Yegg, a California tramp'' origin tale (4 months prior to Sept. 15, 1901 NYT and 3 months prior to Aug. 17, 1901 Literary Digest), which directly contradicts both the Nov. 1899 St. Paul ''John Yegg & Co.'' restitution-letter story and the 1904 ''Swedish tramp'' story.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-112.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-211', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yeggmen', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-05-16', 'https://gahistoricnewspapers.galileo.usg.edu/lccn/sn89053684/1901-05-16/ed-1/seq-4/', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-211.webp', 93192, '56d108045a57def879305667ce8197ff5e63ad9326159ddef907f7800a3f3244', '{"id": "CERT-1500-211", "slug": "cert-1500-211", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yeggmen", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "16 May 1901", "sort_date": "1901-05-16", "short_gloss": "yeggmen in Savannah Morning News (Savannah, GA), May 16, 1901", "source_publication": "Savannah Morning News (Savannah, GA), May 16, 1901", "source_archive": "Georgia Historic Newspapers (DLG / GALILEO, sn89053684)", "source_url": "https://gahistoricnewspapers.galileo.usg.edu/lccn/sn89053684/1901-05-16/ed-1/seq-4/", "page_and_column": "p. 4", "verbatim_quote": "The especial enemies of the country banks are what Robert Pinkerton calls \"yeggmen.\" The name comes from John Yegg, a California tramp who turned bank burglar. The class is recruited from village loafers, tramps and bums.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "First Pinkerton biographical myth (''John Yegg, a California tramp''), contradicting 1899 St. Paul sneak-thief letter", "analysis_notes": "Cross-shard prosopographical record for the 16 May 1901 Savannah Morning News item (p. 4, col. 3; IIIF page scan verified under CERT-1500-112), attributing ''yeggmen'' to Robert Pinkerton and ''John Yegg, a California tramp who turned bank burglar''—corroborated in The Literary Digest (17 Aug. 1901, CERT-1500-212) and The New York Times (15 Sept. 1901, CERT-1500-213), and contradicting both the Nov. 1899 St. Paul sneak-thief note and the 1904 gypsy and Swedish stories.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-211.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-208', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'externally_recognized', 1901, '1901-06-01', 'https://archive.org/details/cu31924030315943/page/n42/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-208.webp', 99236, 'd7122e699f345a4fdde79db57d73d60490e32ea9841a7f8eb95a9d7ea80a9de2', '{"id": "CERT-1500-208", "slug": "cert-1500-208", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "externally_recognized", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": "Cited in Online Etymology Dictionary and Green''s Dictionary of Slang (Josiah Flynt, The World of Graft, 1901, p. 27); primary scan verified", "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "Jun 1901", "sort_date": "1901-06-01", "short_gloss": "yegg in Josiah Flynt, The World of Graft (New York: McClure, Phillips & Co., MCMI [1901])", "source_publication": "Josiah Flynt, The World of Graft (New York: McClure, Phillips & Co., MCMI [1901])", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (cu31924030315943, leaves 8, 42)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924030315943/page/n42/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 27", "verbatim_quote": "The great majority are what certain detectives call \"yegg-men,\" which is a term, by the way, that the detectives would do well to define. Hoboes that break safes in country post-offices come under the yegg-men classification.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Detective-classified hobo safe-breaker cant", "analysis_notes": "Title page verified: MCMI (1901). Lowercases McClure''s ''Yegg-men'' to ''yegg-men'' and adds footnote glosses for ''sneaks'' and ''peter-men'' (safe-blowers).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-208.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-113', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yeggmen', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-08-13', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_new-york-times_1901-08-13_50_16099/page/n11/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-113.webp', 212260, 'c1163ba569565d8d2b0c82b4189d15883da026effaaafec548132c17bbe11b2a', '{"id": "CERT-1500-113", "slug": "cert-1500-113", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yeggmen", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "13 Aug 1901", "sort_date": "1901-08-13", "short_gloss": "Yeggmen in The New York Times (New York, NY)", "source_publication": "The New York Times (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_new-york-times_1901-08-13_50_16099/page/n11/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 50, No. 16099, p. 12, col. 5 (leaf 11)", "verbatim_quote": "The officials of the Pinkerton Detective Agency said yesterday that the Allenhurst robbery was the work of \"Yeggmen.\" There are thousands of these criminals scattered throughout the Western States", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, n. (1903, -2y). Precedes the better-known Sept. 15, 1901 NYT magazine feature by one month (and preceded in NYT Book Review, 27 July 1901, https://archive.org/details/sim_new-york-times_1901-07-27_50_supplement, and Aug. 12, 1900 NYT, CERT-1500-108).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-113.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
