St. Paul sneak-thief note and W. A. Pinkerton''s 1904 gypsy claim.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-212.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-114', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yeggs', 'attestation', 'prior_art_baseline', 'externally_recognized', 1901, '1901-09-15', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_new-york-times_1901-09-15_51_supplement/page/n5/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-114.webp', 144470, 'ed4f75afcf392e79410215531528e94281058d5c1fbbe8d4aaa57ba1dcca0c38', '{"id": "CERT-1500-114", "slug": "cert-1500-114", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yeggs", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "prior_art_baseline", "verification_level": "externally_recognized", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": "Cited as earliest evidence in Merriam-Webster Online (s.v. yegg: 15 Sept. 1901 New York Times Illustrated Magazine Supplement, p. 7); primary scan verified", "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "15 Sep 1901", "sort_date": "1901-09-15", "short_gloss": "Yeggs in The New York Times Illustrated Magazine Supplement (New York, NY)", "source_publication": "The New York Times Illustrated Magazine Supplement (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_new-york-times_1901-09-15_51_supplement/page/n5/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 51, Supplement, p. 7, cols. 1-2 (leaf 6)", "verbatim_quote": "AN invasion of the Eastern States by bands of \"Yeggs\" is a danger which Detective Robert Pinkerton is preparing to meet. ... A \"Yegg\" is a bank burglar of a new type.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, n. (1903, -2y). Primary-scan verification of the exact Sept. 15, 1901 New York Times feature (''A Bank Burglars'' Union: Story of the \"Yeggmen\" and Their Expert Operations With Nitroglycerine'') referenced as Merriam-Webster''s 1901 baseline.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-114.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
