YORK TIMES, SEPTEMBER 15, 1901. 7''. Interviews Robert Pinkerton and Asst. Supt. George S. Dougherty; attests ''Yeggmen''s union'', ''John Yegg'', ''Yeggs'', and ''Yegg talk''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-213.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-215', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yegg men', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1901, '1901-11-07', 'https://archive.org/details/casjhsj_000358/page/n56/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-215.webp', 84384, '8d0e2bbbf7315bac13f81d268bd1e16b88fd744f5d3593c72f48d457c7b2e169', '{"id": "CERT-1500-215", "slug": "cert-1500-215", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yegg men", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1901, "date_display": "7 Nov 1901", "sort_date": "1901-11-07", "short_gloss": "Yegg men in U.S. Penitentiary (Fort Leavenworth, KS) Escape Reward Circulars signed R. W. McClaughry, Warden, in Santa Clara County Sheriff''", "source_publication": "U.S. Penitentiary (Fort Leavenworth, KS) Escape Reward Circulars signed R. W. McClaughry, Warden, in Santa Clara County Sheriff''s Office Wanted Fliers", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (casjhsj_000358, leaves 56, 58)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/casjhsj_000358/page/n56/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Scrapbook pp. 59 & 61 (leaves 56 & 58)", "verbatim_quote": "ESCAPED FROM THE UNITED STATES PENITENTIARY, AT FORT LEAVENWORTH, KANSAS, AT 3.30 P. M., ON NOVEMBER 7TH., 1901... These two men are what are called \"Yegg men\" and they made it a business robbing Country Post Offices, Banks and Railroad Depots.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1901, "masthead_year": 1901, "linguistic_note": "Federal penitentiary institutional adoption of ''Yegg men'' (Warden R. W. McClaughry, former Pinkerton/Bertillon pioneer)", "analysis_notes": "Physical wanted circulars pasted into Santa Clara Sheriff''s scrapbook for escaped federal convicts James Seymore (No. 2176, sentenced May 18, 1900) and Frank Lawrence (No. 2467, sentenced May 8, 1901), both escaped Nov. 7, 1901.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-215.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1901 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-115', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yeggs', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1902, '1902-07-28', 'https://archive.org/details/per_chicago-daily-tribune_1902-07-28_61_209/page/n3/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-115.webp', 257246, '9eaf58c85705e241dcb2f9361f3fb8568ec90474a970dab35438e252010b9f34', '{"id": "CERT-1500-115", "slug": "cert-1500-115", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yeggs", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1902, "date_display": "28 Jul 1902", "sort_date": "1902-07-28", "short_gloss": "Yeggs in The Chicago Daily Tribune (Chicago, IL)", "source_publication": "The Chicago Daily Tribune (Chicago, IL)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_chicago-daily-tribune_1902-07-28_61_209/page/n3/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 61, No. 209, p. 4, col. 3 (leaf 4)", "verbatim_quote": "The men belong to a class of crooks known in their own and the police vernacular as \"Yeggs\"—a bad lot, even in the classification of professional criminal chasers.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1902, "masthead_year": 1902, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, n. (23 June 1903 NY Evening Post, -1y). Corroborated the next day in Pittsburgh Weekly Gazette (29 July 1902), Atlanta Constitution (9 Aug. 1902, ''The \"yegg\" is a tramp who resorts to highway robbery, safe-blowing''), and Los Angeles Times (10 Aug. 1902).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-115.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1902 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-214', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Johnny Yegg', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1903, '1903-02-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_bankers-monthly_1903-02_25_2/page/n33/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-214.webp', 116662, '5287ece03dfc9fdedda312f649b15954f77c13ff2bb3accf411e2e1e6249cc9e', '{"id": "CERT-1500-214", "slug": "cert-1500-214", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Johnny Yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1903, "date_display": "Feb 1903", "sort_date": "1903-02-01", "short_gloss": "Johnny Yegg in The Rand-McNally Bankers'' Monthly (Chicago), Vol. 25, No. 2 (Feb. 1903)", "source_publication": "The Rand-McNally Bankers'' Monthly (Chicago), Vol. 25, No. 2 (Feb. 1903)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_bankers-monthly_1903-02_25_2, leaves 0, 33)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_bankers-monthly_1903-02_25_2/page/n33/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 113, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "As crime after crime was perpetrated by this method the crooks and the police got to saying: \"That''s another Yegg job,\" and so the name of Johnny Yegg goes down to posterity.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1903, "masthead_year": 1903, "linguistic_note": "Colloquial personification ''Johnny Yegg'' alongside plural ''yeggs'' and ''yegg men''", "analysis_notes": "Cover masthead verified: Volume 25, Chicago, February, 1903, Number 2. Antedates OED''s June 23, 1903 Evening Post citation by 4 months and documents the idiomatic phrase ''another Yegg job'' -> ''Johnny Yegg''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-214.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1903 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-205', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg men', 'contextual_evidence', 'corpus_or_prosopographical_control', 'agent_verified', 1903, '1903-07-12', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_los-angeles-times_the-los-angeles-times_1903-07-12/page/n52/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-205.webp', 163574, '6ba800851e4ff93914af184c27737d8179e9935581271d9cf08650eef1736204', '{"id": "CERT-1500-205", "slug": "cert-1500-205", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg men", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "corpus_or_prosopographical_control", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1903, "date_display": "12 Jul 1903", "sort_date": "1903-07-12", "short_gloss": "Contextual Evidence: yegg men (The Los Angeles Times, Illustrated Magazine Section (July 12, 1903), John Elfreth Watkins, Jr., ''Nitro in Cri", "source_publication": "The Los Angeles Times, Illustrated Magazine Section (July 12, 1903), John Elfreth Watkins, Jr., ''Nitro in Crime''", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_los-angeles-times_the-los-angeles-times_1903-07-12, leaf 52)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_los-angeles-times_the-los-angeles-times_1903-07-12/page/n52/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Illustrated Magazine Section, p. 5, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "One reason why the \"nitro\" jobs are now most frequent in the rural territory of the \"yegg men\" cannot be overlooked... \"please keep your sign where honest grafters can see it, as the American Bankers'' Association is too tough for poor grafters. Yours respectfully John Yegg & Co.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1903, "masthead_year": 1903, "linguistic_note": "Facetious corporate pseudonym ''John Yegg & Co.'' echoing generic underworld ''John Yegg'' / ''Johnny Yegg''", "analysis_notes": "Preserves verbatim wording of the Nov. 1899 Scandinavian-American Bank of St. Paul $540 restitution note. The ''& Co.'' suffix confirms a jocular collective alias adopted by urban sneak thieves rather than a real personal name.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-205.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1903 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-216', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yegg man', 'rejected_lead', 'uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology', 'agent_verified', 1903, '1903-09-03', 'https://archive.org/details/ypsilanti_sentinel-commercial_1903.09.03/page/n5/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-216.webp', 173824, 'b36e936ae27ff5139f5bd233fb5443ab537e30b28061cbda86de7901b8e7bc10', '{"id": "CERT-1500-216", "slug": "cert-1500-216", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yegg man", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1903, "date_display": "3 Sep 1903", "sort_date": "1903-09-03", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: Yegg man (The Ypsilanti Sentinel-Commercial (Ypsilanti, MI), Sept. 3, 1903, ''Directory of Beggars'')", "source_publication": "The Ypsilanti Sentinel-Commercial (Ypsilanti, MI), Sept. 3, 1903, ''Directory of Beggars''", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (ypsilanti_sentinel-commercial_1903.09.03, leaves 0, 5)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/ypsilanti_sentinel-commercial_1903.09.03/page/n5/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 6 (leaf 5), col. 4", "verbatim_quote": "He is usually of the variety known as a \"Yegg man\" or tramp safe blower, the name having originated at the time of the arrest of John W. Yegg, the first traveling safe blower known to the police.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1903, "masthead_year": 1903, "linguistic_note": "Falsified pseudo-precision (''John W. Yegg'', Variant 2)", "analysis_notes": "Masthead verified: Sept. 3, 1903 (also syndicated in Dixon Evening Telegraph Sept. 10, 1903 and Griffin Daily News Nov. 6, 1903). Shows real-time fabrication of biographical details (''W.'') for a non-existent founder.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-216.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1903 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-217', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yeggs', 'attestation', 'prior_art_baseline', 'externally_recognized', 1904, '1904-03-06', 'https://www.historicalcrimedetective.com/vtcs1/pdf/ch5-6.pdf', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-217.webp', 144634, '0d192ce3ac7104699504a150a7def7cf248567a0a9fab4b35df8cf85af74b437', '{"id": "CERT-1500-217", "slug": "cert-1500-217", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yeggs", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "prior_art_baseline", "verification_level": "externally_recognized", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": "Investigated in Barry A. Popik & Gerald L. Cohen, Studies in Slang, vol. 6 (Forum Anglicum, vol. 24, Peter Lang, 1999), pp. 21–26 (6 Mar. 1904 St. Louis Post-Dispatch Reading Railroad ''John Yeager'' account)", "publication_year": 1904, "date_display": "6 Mar 1904", "sort_date": "1904-03-06", "short_gloss": "Yeggs in St. Louis Post-Dispatch, Sunday Magazine (March 6, 1904), ''Nemesis in the Camera'' with signed statement ''BY WILLIAM A. PINKERTON''", "source_publication": "St. Louis Post-Dispatch, Sunday Magazine (March 6, 1904), ''Nemesis in the Camera'' with signed statement ''BY WILLIAM A. PINKERTON''", "source_archive": "Historical Crime Detective Archival PDF (vtcs1/pdf/ch5-6.pdf, p. 1)", "source_url": "https://www.historicalcrimedetective.com/vtcs1/pdf/ch5-6.pdf", "page_and_column": "Sunday Magazine, p. 4, cols. 3-4", "verbatim_quote": "The \"Yeggs\" were originated some years ago by a tramp burglar named John Yeager, whose band robbed and burglarized along the length of the Reading railroad.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1904, "masthead_year": 1904, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Reading Railroad ''Yeager'' (< Jager) + generic common-noun ''a John Yegg, or leader''", "analysis_notes": "Visual inspection of PDF pixels reveals Acrobat ClearScan vector-font substitution on body newsprint alongside original halftone Bertillon photos; conservatively graded BASELINE-LITERATURE . Attests both Reading RR ''John Yeager'' and generic title ''Rudolph was a John Yegg'' / ''band had a John Yegg, or leader''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-217.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1904 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-218', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yeggman', 'rejected_lead', 'uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology', 'agent_verified', 1904, '1904-09-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_american-lawyer-1893_1904-09_12/page/n9/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-218.webp', 156926, '710202d2c78a0f7f8f4ec1faf674831ea3c76b19ee56ba1066c1f3f90eda2b8d', '{"id": "CERT-1500-218", "slug": "cert-1500-218", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yeggman", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1904, "date_display": "Sep 1904", "sort_date": "1904-09-01", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: Yeggman (William A. Pinkerton, ''The Yeggman'' (read at IACP Convention, St. Louis, June 6-11, 1904), The American Lawyer, Vol.", "source_publication": "William A. Pinkerton, ''The Yeggman'' (read at IACP Convention, St. Louis, June 6-11, 1904), The American Lawyer, Vol. 12, No. 9 (Sept. 1904)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_american-lawyer-1893_1904-09_12, leaves 8-9)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_american-lawyer-1893_1904-09_12/page/n9/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "pp. 385-386", "verbatim_quote": "When a particularly clever thief is found among a gypsy tribe he is selected as the \"Yegg\" or chief thief... they, using the expression of the gypsies, called him a \"Yegg.\" Then came the name of \"John Yegg\" and finally the word \"Yeggman.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1904, "masthead_year": 1904, "linguistic_note": "W. A. Pinkerton''s self-contradictory Gypsy ''Yegg'' folk etymology (paired with ''Ho-Beau -> hobo'')", "analysis_notes": "Devastating internal contradiction: W. A. Pinkerton (1) attests reading a paper on ''the Yeggman'' at the May 1900 Cincinnati IACP convention, and (2) discards BOTH the 1899 St. Paul sneak-thief note and Robert Pinkerton''s 1901 California hobo story, claiming ''Yegg'' preceded ''John Yegg''!", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-218.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1904 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-220', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yeggmen', 'rejected_lead', 'uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology', 'agent_verified', 1904, '1904-09-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_everybodys-magazine_1904-09_11_3/page/n137/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-220.webp', 108794, '823224cebcfd6cf3c53aabb1b49027d33756559054425fa8f19f7341758b4648', '{"id": "CERT-1500-220", "slug": "cert-1500-220", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yeggmen", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1904, "date_display": "Sep 1904", "sort_date": "1904-09-01", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: yeggmen (Everybody''s Magazine, Vol. 11, No. 3 (Sept. 1904), p. 424 (corroborated against Sept. 5, 1908 South SF Enterprise ''C", "source_publication": "Everybody''s Magazine, Vol. 11, No. 3 (Sept. 1904), p. 424 (corroborated against Sept. 5, 1908 South SF Enterprise ''Coldwater, Mich.'' myth)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_everybodys-magazine_1904-09_11_3, leaves 0, 137; cssf_000677, leaf 3)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_everybodys-magazine_1904-09_11_3/page/n137/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 424, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "The words \"yeggs\" and \"yeggmen\" have crept into the newspapers, but they are still mysterious to most of us... They are named after John Yegg, a Swede, who belongs to Bacon''s first class of great men", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1904, "masthead_year": 1904, "linguistic_note": "Mutating ethnic/occupational folklore (Swedish safe-breaker Variant 4; Coldwater electrician Variant 5)", "analysis_notes": "Shows how within five years ''John Yegg'' mutated across incompatible nationalities and biographies (St. Paul sneak alias, California hobo, Reading RR Yeager, Gypsy chief, Swede, Coldwater electrician)—classic hallmark of retrospective eponym mythmaking.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-220.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1904 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-219', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yegg', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1904, '1904-12-25', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_new-york-times_1904-12-25_54_17153/page/n18/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-219.webp', 202342, '4e7128b606a39accbb1e14187fdb13ba54fe74c99bd9dd642a5a431d3332d2c0', '{"id": "CERT-1500-219", "slug": "cert-1500-219", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1904, "date_display": "25 Dec 1904", "sort_date": "1904-12-25", "short_gloss": "Yegg in The New York Times (Sunday, Dec. 25, 1904), ''New York''s Holiday Beggar and His Graft''", "source_publication": "The New York Times (Sunday, Dec. 25, 1904), ''New York''s Holiday Beggar and His Graft''", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_new-york-times_1904-12-25_54_17153, leaves 0, 18)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_new-york-times_1904-12-25_54_17153/page/n18/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Magazine Section, p. 3 (leaf 18), col. 3", "verbatim_quote": "The following is a brief glossary of beggars'' slang: One cent.—Indian... Safe blower.—Pete-man. Detective in citizen''s clothes.—Bull. Uniformed policeman.—Bull in harness. Beggar.—John-bum, or John-Yegg.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1904, "masthead_year": 1904, "linguistic_note": "Productive underworld ''John-X'' generic personification (''John-bum, or John-Yegg'', cf. ''John Law'', ''John Family'')", "analysis_notes": "Masthead and running head verified: Sunday, Dec. 25, 1904. Demonstrates morphologically that ''John-Yegg'' belonged to the productive American tramp ''John-X'' prefix series alongside ''John-bum''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-219.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1904 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-223', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'Yegg', 'rejected_lead', 'misdated_source', 'agent_verified', 1905, '1905-03-30', 'https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_35otAAAAIAAJ/page/n638/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-223.webp', 103094, '1ba0b64bb5aca2c1ede6fcc881cb52398d2bb222002141cc85ceef615187c4f2', '{"id": "CERT-1500-223", "slug": "cert-1500-223", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "Yegg", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "misdated_source", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1905, "date_display": "30 Mar 1905", "sort_date": "1905-03-30", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: Yegg (Hans Gross (ed.), Archiv fur Kriminal-Anthropologie und Kriminalistik, Bd. 18 (Leipzig: F. C. W. Vogel, 1905), ''XI. Ame", "source_publication": "Hans Gross (ed.), Archiv fur Kriminal-Anthropologie und Kriminalistik, Bd. 18 (Leipzig: F. C. W. Vogel, 1905), ''XI. Amerikanische Bankrauber. Von William A. Pinkerton''", "source_archive": "Internet Archive / Google Books (bub_gb_35otAAAAIAAJ, leaves 392, 634, 638)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_35otAAAAIAAJ/page/n638/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Bd. 18, pp. 223, 228", "verbatim_quote": "Das Wort \"Yegg\" stammt von den Zigeunern... nannten sie ihn nach Zigeunerart einen Yegg; daraus wurde spater John Yegg und schliesslich Yeggman.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1905, "masthead_year": 1905, "linguistic_note": "Trap A ghost-antedating shield (kills false 1899 German criminological citation)", "analysis_notes": "Google Books / IA metadata stamps ''1899'' from Vol. 1 of Gross''s Archiv, but Bd. 18''s title page (leaf 392) explicitly prints ''1905'' and p. 223 tabulates bank burglaries ''von September 1900 bis 1904'' (translating Pinkerton''s June 1904 St. Louis address).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-223.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1905 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-116', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegging', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1905, '1905-06-02', 'https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_st-louis-post-dispatch_1905-06-02_57_285/page/n3/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-116.webp', 150726, '268cc5d941bf5ec825e4b3e182efeed1a09b19408647fd3b0b7d9c30e245102a', '{"id": "CERT-1500-116", "slug": "cert-1500-116", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegging", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1905, "date_display": "2 Jun 1905", "sort_date": "1905-06-02", "short_gloss": "yegging in St. Louis Post-Dispatch (St. Louis, MO)", "source_publication": "St. Louis Post-Dispatch (St. Louis, MO)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_st-louis-post-dispatch_1905-06-02_57_285/page/n3/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 57, No. 285, p. 4, col. 4 (leaf 4)", "verbatim_quote": "On the whole, though, he prefers the avocation of beggar as involving less exertion and less risk than \"log rolling\" or \"yegging.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1905, "masthead_year": 1905, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, v. (1916, Jack Lait; 11-year antedating!). Genuine deverbal gerund ''yegging'' (''operating as a safecracking yegg / robber'', contrasted with ''log rolling'' = robbing drunks and ''locates jobs for safe blowers'' in the preceding sentence).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-116.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1905 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-206', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'William Barrett', 'contextual_evidence', 'corpus_or_prosopographical_control', 'agent_verified', 1905, '1905-10-10', 'https://archive.org/details/proceedingsofann31amer/page/n79/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-206.webp', 60280, '74584dd283fb8622c41412203f82a7a6d5eed95c528720c5806f63d84ebbb5b4', '{"id": "CERT-1500-206", "slug": "cert-1500-206", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "William Barrett", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "corpus_or_prosopographical_control", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1905, "date_display": "10 Oct 1905", "sort_date": "1905-10-10", "short_gloss": "Contextual Evidence: William Barrett (Proceedings of the Thirty-First Annual Convention of the American Bankers'' Association (Washington, D.", "source_publication": "Proceedings of the Thirty-First Annual Convention of the American Bankers'' Association (Washington, D.C., Oct. 10-13, 1905), Pinkerton Report", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (proceedingsofann31amer, leaves 9, 79, 97)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/proceedingsofann31amer/page/n79/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "pp. 35-36, 55", "verbatim_quote": "robbery was committed by William Barrett, a professional, whose portrait (345S) we had sent to members in bulletin No. 4; also learned that he, with Fritzie Dhien and G. H. Hanlon, two professional bank sneaks, were on the Pacific Coast, and warned the various police departments of this, as a result of which all three were arrested at Portland, Ore., on May 1.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1905, "masthead_year": 1905, "linguistic_note": "Prosopographical falsification of William Barrett as a tramp safecracker", "analysis_notes": "Title page verified: 1905 (IA catalog misdates serial to 1875). Proves William Barrett (Portrait 345S) was an elite urban bank sneak thief who stole $20,000 in gold from the First National Bank of San Francisco, operated with bank sneaks Fritzie Dhien and G. H. Hanlon, was arrested May 1, 1905 in Portland, OR, and served 2 yrs. 3 mos. in the Maryland Penitentiary under ''Sneak Thieves''—strictly segregated from the report''s 21 ''yegg'' safe-burglar entries.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-206.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1905 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-123', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yeggman', 'rejected_lead', 'misdated_source', 'agent_verified', 1906, '1906-01-27', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_scientific-american_1906-01-27_94_4/page/n2/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-123.webp', 102394, 'c18c2107e333a7fdf9b2ccb4fb485207a8c2db1ea23aca05df44bcd857700e5a', '{"id": "CERT-1500-123", "slug": "cert-1500-123", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yeggman", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "misdated_source", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1906, "date_display": "27 Jan 1906", "sort_date": "1906-01-27", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: yeggman (Scientific American (New York, NY))", "source_publication": "Scientific American (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_scientific-american_1906-01-27_94_4/page/n2/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 94, No. 4, p. 88 (leaf 3)", "verbatim_quote": "no safe is safe from the peripatetic yeggman—in daylight the harmless vagrant, and at night the terror of the country bank official", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1906, "masthead_year": 1906, "linguistic_note": "", "analysis_notes": "Trap A Falsification: On Jan. 2, 2020, Scientific American reprinted excerpts of ''The Ungentle Art of Burglary'' under ''Originally published in January 1856'', creating a viral 1856 ''yeggman'' ghost date. Physical masthead inspection proves publication on Jan. 27, 1906 (Vol. 94, No. 4, p. 88). Also logs IA bound-serial catalog misdates: proceedingsofann30amer (cat. 1875 -> actual 1904 ABA Proceedings), booknotesv19prov (cat. 1883 -> actual 1902), dialectnotes02newhuoft (cat. 1890 -> actual 1904), and bub_gb_35otAAAAIAAJ (Archiv fuer Kriminologie, cat. 1899 -> actual 1905).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-123.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1906 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-117', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1906, '1906-06-09', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1906-06-09_50_1286/page/n4/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-117.webp', 71672, '4bbbaeb9343b5480b327142791b506f0cf2d4584c48fa3fab90d1486d7609705', '{"id": "CERT-1500-117", "slug": "cert-1500-117", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1906, "date_display": "9 Jun 1906", "sort_date": "1906-06-09", "short_gloss": "yegg in Judge (New York, NY)", "source_publication": "Judge (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1906-06-09_50_1286/page/n4/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 50, No. 1286, leaf 5", "verbatim_quote": "Why, the robber! ... Why doesn''t he chloroform us if he is [going] to yegg the game from us that way? Is that the umpire who was reported to [have] had brain-fever last winter? Why, he can prove an alibi on that charge.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1906, "masthead_year": 1906, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, v. (1916, Jack Lait; 10-year antedating!). Unambiguous transitive infinitive ''to yegg [the game from us]'' (''to rob/steal brazenly like a yeggman'', reinforced by ''Why, the robber!'' and ''chloroform us'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-117.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1906 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-221', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'contextual_evidence', 'corpus_or_prosopographical_control', 'agent_verified', 1906, '1906-10-16', 'https://archive.org/details/americanbankersa0000jame/page/n83/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-221.webp', 89682, 'c5465d625b848ae85050c613fc5f6433c3eb52576ebf1f697ae1db0117dd447e', '{"id": "CERT-1500-221", "slug": "cert-1500-221", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "corpus_or_prosopographical_control", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1906, "date_display": "16 Oct 1906", "sort_date": "1906-10-16", "short_gloss": "Contextual Evidence: yegg (Proceedings of the Thirty-Second Annual Convention of the American Bankers'' Association (St. Louis, Oct. 16-19, 1", "source_publication": "Proceedings of the Thirty-Second Annual Convention of the American Bankers'' Association (St. Louis, Oct. 16-19, 1906), Pinkerton Report", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (americanbankersa0000jame, leaves 9, 83)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/americanbankersa0000jame/page/n83/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 51 (leaf 83)", "verbatim_quote": "Thomas James, alias \"The Rambler,\" is one of the original \"yegg\" men, and among the first who operated upon safes with explosives.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1906, "masthead_year": 1906, "linguistic_note": "Empirical Pinkerton case-file proof naming real pioneer nitroglycerin safecrackers by road moniker", "analysis_notes": "Title page verified: Oct. 16-19, 1906. When citing actual case files rather than press folklore, Pinkerton''s ABA reports identify real early explosive safecrackers like Thomas James (''The Rambler'', killed Feb. 4, 1906) and never record any convict named ''John Yegg''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-221.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1906 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-224', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'rejected_lead', 'misdated_source', 'agent_verified', 1907, '1907-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/pt2dictionaryeng00brynuoft/page/n1025/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-224.webp', 120768, 'b46760d5b2faf2bbf576797c2557d1c57c2304731b59a8393f6a30ffa14cd182', '{"id": "CERT-1500-224", "slug": "cert-1500-224", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "misdated_source", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1907, "date_display": "1907", "sort_date": "1907-01-01", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: yegg (John Brynildsen, A Dictionary of the English and Dano-Norwegian Languages, Vol. II (Copenhagen: Gyldendal, 1907 [cat. 1", "source_publication": "John Brynildsen, A Dictionary of the English and Dano-Norwegian Languages, Vol. II (Copenhagen: Gyldendal, 1907 [cat. 1886/1902]) & Sidney S. Rider, Book Notes, Vol. 19 (1902 [cat. 1883])", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (pt2dictionaryeng00brynuoft leaf 1025; in.ernet.dli.2015.88943; booknotesv19prov leaf 7; proceedingsofann30amer)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/pt2dictionaryeng00brynuoft/page/n1025/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Brynildsen Vol. II, p. 1011; Book Notes Vol. 19, pp. 157-158", "verbatim_quote": "yegg [jeg] amr Omstrejfer, Bandit c; Yeggs and Hobos. Ifolge Everybody''s Magazine Sept. 1904 efter John Yegg, en svensk Pengeskabstyv.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1907, "masthead_year": 1907, "linguistic_note": "Trap A ghost-antedating shield (kills 1875, 1883, 1886, and 1902 metadata mirages)", "analysis_notes": "DLI item in.ernet.dli.2015.88943 stamps ''1886'' and Toronto item pt2dictionaryeng00brynuoft stamps ''1902'' (fascicle 1 date), yet p. 1011 explicitly cites ''Everybody''s Magazine Sept. 1904''! Similarly, booknotesv19prov (''1883'') is Vol. XIX (1902), and proceedingsofann30amer (''1875'') is Vol. 30 (1904).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-224.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1907 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-118', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1908, '1908-06-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_everybodys-magazine_1908-06_18_6/page/n35/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-118.webp', 126608, '6f9ee0c980d9807ca5746636971e9334d85a662dda789413281c2b5e1abf092c', '{"id": "CERT-1500-118", "slug": "cert-1500-118", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1908, "date_display": "Jun 1908", "sort_date": "1908-06-01", "short_gloss": "yegg in Everybody''s Magazine (New York, NY)", "source_publication": "Everybody''s Magazine (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_everybodys-magazine_1908-06_18_6/page/n35/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 18, No. 6, p. 726, col. 1 (leaf 36)", "verbatim_quote": "When at last the doors opened to set him free, a guard said to him: \"Well, I suppose you are going to yegg it.\" And George said: \"By God, I am.\" He did. He went back to Atlanta and turned burglar.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1908, "masthead_year": 1908, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, v. (1916, Jack Lait; 8-year antedating!). Clear verbal construction ''going to yegg it'' (''practice burglary as a yegg''), immediately glossed in the next sentence: ''He went back to Atlanta and turned burglar.''", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-118.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1908 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-222', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'sneak', 'contextual_evidence', 'corpus_or_prosopographical_control', 'agent_verified', 1908, '1908-12-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_american-bankers-association-aba-banking-journal_1908-12_1_6/page/n11/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-222.webp', 66764, 'd6bd654ef0ace27465386c5c61c23bbe9f583e209a76bf31572bcff2ff41498e', '{"id": "CERT-1500-222", "slug": "cert-1500-222", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "sneak", "record_type": "contextual_evidence", "record_subtype": "corpus_or_prosopographical_control", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1908, "date_display": "Dec 1908", "sort_date": "1908-12-01", "short_gloss": "Contextual Evidence: sneak (Journal of the American Bankers'' Association, Vol. 1, No. 6 (Dec. 1908), pp. 189-190 (+ 1870-1905 IA Directory &", "source_publication": "Journal of the American Bankers'' Association, Vol. 1, No. 6 (Dec. 1908), pp. 189-190 (+ 1870-1905 IA Directory & Prison Register FTS)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (sim_american-bankers-association-aba-banking-journal_1908-12_1_6, leaves 0, 11)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_american-bankers-association-aba-banking-journal_1908-12_1_6/page/n11/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "pp. 189-190", "verbatim_quote": "When the cashier of a St. Paul bank balanced his accounts one night there was a shortage of $540... \"Why don''t you keep your sign out?\"... Every safebreaker, forger and \"sneak\" in the United States knows", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1908, "masthead_year": 1908, "linguistic_note": "Onomastic null result: 0 historical persons or convicts named ''John Yegg'' in 1870-1905 registers/directories", "analysis_notes": "Even the ABA''s own 1908 journal reprinted a distorted press version of the St. Paul $540 return without ''John Yegg''. Corpus-wide IA FTS for ''Yegg, John'' across all digitized 1870-1905 city directories and prison reports returns 0 pre-1957 individuals.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-222.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1908 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-225', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'attestation', 'prior_art_baseline', 'externally_recognized', 1909, '1909-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/centurydictionar12whituoft/page/n719/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-225.webp', 99204, '35ba222def38c5e1b3806d2c091d3dee31e8be6d17d8494b80ad7baa0721c5d3', '{"id": "CERT-1500-225", "slug": "cert-1500-225", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "prior_art_baseline", "verification_level": "externally_recognized", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-B", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": "Published in The Century Dictionary Supplement, Vol. XII (1909), p. 1459/1462, s.v. yegg & yeggman (preserving OED1''s 23 June 1903 New York Evening Post baseline and proposing *yegger < German Jäger)", "publication_year": 1909, "date_display": "1909", "sort_date": "1909-01-01", "short_gloss": "yegg in The Century Dictionary Supplement, Vol. XII (New York: The Century Co., copyright 1909), s.v. yegg & yeggman", "source_publication": "The Century Dictionary Supplement, Vol. XII (New York: The Century Co., copyright 1909), s.v. yegg & yeggman", "source_archive": "Internet Archive (centurydictionar12whituoft, leaves 12, 719)", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/centurydictionar12whituoft/page/n719/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. XII, p. 1459, col. 2", "verbatim_quote": "yegg (yeg), n. [Origin obscure: said to be from the name (John Yegg) of a tramp and safe-breaker; poss., through the form *yegger, < G. jager, hunter.] Same as *yeggman.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1909, "masthead_year": 1909, "linguistic_note": "Early scholarly formulation of German Jager > *yegger > yegg alongside skeptical ''said to be from (John Yegg)''", "analysis_notes": "Copyright leaf verified: 1909. Supplies the exact June 23, 1903 N.Y. Evening Post quotation (via Dialect Notes II.vi) later copied as OED''s 1903 baseline, and already proposes back-formation via *yegger < German Jager.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-225.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1909 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-303', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegg', 'attestation', 'prior_art_baseline', 'externally_recognized', 1909, '1909-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/centurydictionar0012benj/page/n716/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-303.webp', 109624, '97b966ebc3adc4b0b807f482ff376e948270ed72e6dbac89027fecfd83d7ac09', '{"id": "CERT-1500-303", "slug": "cert-1500-303", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegg", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "prior_art_baseline", "verification_level": "externally_recognized", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-C", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": "Published in The Century Dictionary Supplement, Vol. XII (1909), p. 1462, s.v. yegg & yeggman (reconstructing *yegger < German Jäger, hunter)", "publication_year": 1909, "date_display": "1909", "sort_date": "1909-01-01", "short_gloss": "yegg in Benjamin E. Smith (ed.), The Century Dictionary and Cyclopedia, Vol. XII: The Century Dictionary Supplement (New York: The Century C", "source_publication": "Benjamin E. Smith (ed.), The Century Dictionary and Cyclopedia, Vol. XII: The Century Dictionary Supplement (New York: The Century Co., copyright 1909 [1910 issue]), p. 1462, col. 2 (leaf n716, s.v. ''yegg'' & ''yeggman'')", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/centurydictionar0012benj/page/n716/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. XII (Supplement), p. 1462, col. 2 (leaf n716)", "verbatim_quote": "yegg (yeg), n. [Origin obscure: said to be from the name (John Yegg) of a tramp and safe-breaker; poss., through the form *yegger, < G. jäger, hunter.] Same as *yeggman. The prompt breaking up of the organized gangs of professional beggars and yeggs. N. Y. Evening Post, June 23, 1903. Quoted in Dialect Notes, II. vi. // yeggman (yeg''man), n.; pl. yeggmen (-men). [yegg + man.] A tramp burglar and safe-breaker.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1909, "masthead_year": 1909, "linguistic_note": "Earliest authoritative dictionary etymology of yegg (1909), recording only (1) the Pinkerton ''John Yegg'' eponym story and (2) a conjectured morphological back-formation ''poss., through the form *yegger, < G. jäger, hunter''—notably free of any San Francisco Chinatown / Cantonese ''yek'' claim, and independently corroborated by the unasterisked 1893 Hartford Courant rail-tramp attestation ''yeager''.", "analysis_notes": "BASELINE-LITERATURE BENCHMARK (Donor-Lexicon Audit): Primary scan of The Century Dictionary Supplement (centurydictionar0012benj, leaf n6 title page, leaf n7 ''two new volumes in 1909'', leaf n716 p. 1462 col. 2) proves two critical historiographical facts: (1) contrary to later popular retellings, the 1909 Century Supplement did NOT advance the Chinatown ''yek'' myth; (2) Century''s philologists explicitly reconstructed an asterisked intermediate ''*yegger < G. jäger, hunter'' from pure morphological reasoning—a prediction strikingly validated by the actual 1893 Hartford Courant form ''yeager'' and 1908 Arthur Stringer / 1925 Jim Tully ''yegger''.", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-303.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1909 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-119', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegging', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1909, '1909-01-16', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1909-01-16_181_29/page/n9/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-119.webp', 95840, '9fc8ad97ad28b0adb014789544069d55961edd063ef13dd2c0ab5d3dac486846', '{"id": "CERT-1500-119", "slug": "cert-1500-119", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegging", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1909, "date_display": "16 Jan 1909", "sort_date": "1909-01-16", "short_gloss": "yegging in The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia, PA)", "source_publication": "The Saturday Evening Post (Philadelphia, PA)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_saturday-evening-post_1909-01-16_181_29/page/n9/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 181, No. 29, p. 8, col. 2 (leaf 10)", "verbatim_quote": "\"Oh, it''s a great game, all right.\" \"It''s got yegging frazzled to a pulp,\" agreed Wallingford. \"But I oughtn''t to yell police.\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1909, "masthead_year": 1909, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, v. (1916, Jack Lait; 7-year antedating!). George Randolph Chester''s Get-Rich-Quick Wallingford story (reprinted in Young Wallingford, 1910, https://archive.org/details/youngwallingford00chesiala), contrasting confidence swindling with ''yegging'' (safecracking).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-119.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1909 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-120', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegged', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1910, '1910-03-01', 'https://archive.org/details/sim_everybodys-magazine_1910-03_22_3/page/n39/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-120.webp', 99408, '10d21c3ad121e049973b2b9b3d57ee36f4db226f394912e91df117d0585e33fb', '{"id": "CERT-1500-120", "slug": "cert-1500-120", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegged", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1910, "date_display": "Mar 1910", "sort_date": "1910-03-01", "short_gloss": "yegged in Everybody''s Magazine (New York, NY)", "source_publication": "Everybody''s Magazine (New York, NY)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/sim_everybodys-magazine_1910-03_22_3/page/n39/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 22, No. 3, p. 294, col. 2 (leaf 40)", "verbatim_quote": "Gentleman Dan was at once enlightened. The Romney was a picture. He had once \"yegged it\" with an old Adam Worth gang forger", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1910, "masthead_year": 1910, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, v. (1916, Jack Lait; 6-year antedating!). Earliest verified finite past-tense form ''yegged'' in criminal burglary sense (also reprinted in Pall Mall Magazine, July 1910; followed in 1911 by Talking Machine World: ''walked and yegged (meaning stole) second'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-120.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1910 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-121', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegged', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1912, '1912-09-25', 'https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_1912-09-25_65_36/page/n8/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-121.webp', 184932, '538bef1df0d43978586236e14a1ce9f3e556015e8303a9f8e6709d6ad5119497', '{"id": "CERT-1500-121", "slug": "cert-1500-121", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegged", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1912, "date_display": "25 Sep 1912", "sort_date": "1912-09-25", "short_gloss": "yegged in St. Louis Post-Dispatch (St. Louis, MO)", "source_publication": "St. Louis Post-Dispatch (St. Louis, MO)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_1912-09-25_65_36/page/n8/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Vol. 65, No. 36, p. 9, col. 4 (leaf 9)", "verbatim_quote": "not only to nullify his contract with a club owner, but he can also deprive him of a large negotiable asset just as surely as if he yegged the dough out of a strong box.", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1912, "masthead_year": 1912, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, v. (1916, Jack Lait; 4-year antedating!). Unquoted transitive safecracking past-tense verb ''yegged the dough out of a strong box'' (syndicated in Los Angeles Times, 1 Dec. 1912).", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-121.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1912 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-122', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yegging', 'attestation', 'primary_attestation', 'agent_verified', 1913, '1913-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.168547/page/n98/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-122.webp', 53582, '45181d0328e12b0d68924646616e1cc4c5e35843d656e049bce291b951936527', '{"id": "CERT-1500-122", "slug": "cert-1500-122", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yegging", "record_type": "attestation", "record_subtype": "primary_attestation", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-A", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1913, "date_display": "1913", "sort_date": "1913-01-01", "short_gloss": "yegging in Harold MacGrath, Deuces Wild (Indianapolis: Bobbs-Merrill)", "source_publication": "Harold MacGrath, Deuces Wild (Indianapolis: Bobbs-Merrill)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.168547/page/n98/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "p. 93 (leaf 99; also p. 113 ''yegged safes'')", "verbatim_quote": "Well, this chap''s play was—\" Haggerty arose. \"Will!\" \"Buying up ol'' safes an'' yegging ''em!\"", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1913, "masthead_year": 1913, "linguistic_note": "Pennsylvania German / Rotwelsch Jäger > yagar/yeager (''itinerant rail-tramp / beggar'') shortened in 1890s U.S. rail-tramp cant to yegg/yeggs and applied c. 1897-1899 to tramp nitroglycerine safecrackers", "analysis_notes": "Benchmarked against OED yegg, v. (1916, Jack Lait; 3-year antedating!). Exact literal transitive sense (''cracking safes as a yegg''), paired on p. 113 with ''th'' way you yegged safes for th'' fun o'' th'' thing'', alongside Saturday Evening Post (8 Feb. 1913, ''determined to yegg it'') and MIT Technology Review (July 1913, ''yegging the office safe'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-122.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1913 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO citations (id, target_id, case_slug, run_id, headword, attested_form, record_type, record_subtype, verification_level, publication_year, sort_date, source_url, masthead_date_verified, scan_hosted_path, scan_bytes, scan_sha256, record_json, updated_at) VALUES ('CERT-1500-304', 'TGT-132', 'yegg', NULL, 'yegg', 'yekk', 'rejected_lead', 'uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology', 'agent_verified', 1926, '1926-01-01', 'https://archive.org/details/youcantwin0000jack/page/172/mode/1up', 1, '/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-304.webp', 76150, '584af756c019a3fc47f61c20b0a52a11ef81f38e809260cb1d3d3df2b41a4994', '{"id": "CERT-1500-304", "slug": "cert-1500-304", "case_slug": "yegg", "headword": "yegg", "attested_form": "yekk", "record_type": "rejected_lead", "record_subtype": "uncorroborated_or_folk_etymology", "verification_level": "agent_verified", "verified_by_agent": "DRAgNEt 1500-C", "human_verified_by": null, "human_verified_date": null, "external_recognition": null, "publication_year": 1926, "date_display": "1926", "sort_date": "1926-01-01", "short_gloss": "Rejected Lead: yekk (Jack Black, You Can''t Win, with a Foreword by Robert Herrick (New York: The Macmillan Company, 1926), ch. XIII, p. 172 ", "source_publication": "Jack Black, You Can''t Win, with a Foreword by Robert Herrick (New York: The Macmillan Company, 1926), ch. XIII, p. 172 (leaf n189); cross-checked against T. L. Stedman & K. P. Lee, A Chinese and English Phrase Book in the Canton Dialect ... for the Use of the Chinese Resident in America (New York: William R. Jenkins Co., Copyright 1888), Lesson XXIV, pp. 66–67 (leaves n101–n102)", "source_archive": "Internet Archive", "source_url": "https://archive.org/details/youcantwin0000jack/page/172/mode/1up", "page_and_column": "Jack Black, You Can''t Win (1926), p. 172 (leaf n189); Stedman & Lee (1888), pp. 66–67 (leaves n101–n102)", "verbatim_quote": "[Jack Black, You Can''t Win (1926), p. 172:] In speaking of the cook ovens I may say that it was there the word \"yegg\" originated. It has not yet been locked in the dictionary, but it has a place in our language and it''s about time its derivation was settled once and for all. It is a corruption of \"yekk,\" a word from one of the many dialects spoken in Chinatown, and it means beggar. When a hypo or beggar approached a Chinaman to ask for something to eat, he was greeted with the exclamation, \"yekk man, yekk man.\" [Contrast Stedman & Lee, Canton Dialect Phrase Book (New York, 1888), pp. 66–67:] 11. A thief broke in my shop and stole all I had. / 十二 有賊入舖將我的嘢一概偷哂 (''yau ch''ák yap p''u''...).", "masthead_date_verified": true, "catalog_year": 1926, "masthead_year": 1926, "linguistic_note": "Falsifies the popular San Francisco Chinatown ''yekk = beggar'' origin story popularized by ex-safecracker Jack Black in You Can''t Win (1926): (1) chronologically published 26 years after the 1900 baseline (and 33 years after New England rail-tramp ''yeager'' in the Jan. 23, 1893 Hartford Courant and 32 years after ''yegg'' in the Jan. 14, 1894 Cincinnati Enquirer); (2) Black falsely asserts in 1926 that yegg ''has not yet been locked in the dictionary'' (it had been in Century Supplement 1909 and Webster''s New International 1909 for 17 years); (3) lexically, no Cantonese or Siyi dialect word yekk/yik/yak means ''beggar'' or ''thief''—at Chinatown cook-ovens, yak fán! (喫飯, Williams 1856 p. 674) means ''eat rice / take food!'', which Black retroactively folk-etymologized onto preexisting hobo yeggman.", "analysis_notes": "FALSIFIED-MYTH PRIMARY SOURCE TRACE (Donor-Lexicon Audit): Traces the famous Chinatown ''yekk man = beggar'' anecdote directly to Jack Black''s 1926 memoir You Can''t Win (youcantwin0000jack, leaf n5–n6 Macmillan 1926 title/imprint; leaf n189 p. 172), quoted in Green''s Dictionary of Slang, Grammarphobia, and Slang City. Fails both deterministic gates: chronologically implausible (1926 > 1900; pre-1900 Eastern/Midwestern rail-tramp attestations in CT 1893 and OH 1894 predate Black''s memoir by over three decades) and unattested in historical Cantonese lexicons (Stedman & Lee''s 1888 New York Chinatown phrasebook, leaves n4, n101–n102, confirms U.S. Cantonese speakers used 賊 ch''ák/ts''ák for ''thief'', while cook-shop yak fán means ''eat rice!'').", "scan": {"hosted_path": "/scans/yegg/CERT-1500-304.webp", "rights_status": "us_public_domain_pre_1931", "rights_note": "Published 1926 (<= 1930): public domain in the United States; WebP proof scan hosted directly."}}', '2026-11-27T05:35:25Z');
